osts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T13:23:39-08:00","id":1532105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1532089#post1532089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried to get into Promethean the Created, but playing it was harder than we thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I never played it myself. It seemed like an interesting concept, but I wasn't sure how well it worked in actual play. Maybe I should check it out one of these years...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T12:07:23-07:00","id":1532713,"title":"","content":"The concept of Promethean The Created was solid, but how do you accurately depict such isolation and tragic storytelling? It can be done once in awhile but there are times where you want to see your monsters have something of a good ending.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-17T05:29:53-07:00","id":1532766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1532713#post1532713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The concept of Promethean The Created was solid, but how do you accurately depict such isolation and tragic storytelling? It can be done once in awhile but there are times where you want to see your monsters have something of a good ending.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I get ya. Yea, it's hard to just constantly do bleak stories. Every now and then you need something good to happen...<br /> <br /> To switch gears a bit, not an upcoming movie, but I recently watched Madame Webb. The idea behind it is interesting, but the movie itself is kind of bland. There just isn't a lot that happens in it. Everyone in it is pretty good, but they don't have a lot to work with.<br /> <br /> So, based on this, it's not looking good for that Kraven the Hunter movie.<br /> <br /> Ohhh!! I saw the trailer for that Crow &quot;remake&quot; and whoa..... it does not look good. Well, if this was another Crow story about a different character, then I'd be more on board with it. When I first heard about it a few years back it was pitched as being closer to the story in the original comic rather than a remake of the movie, which I thought sounded pretty cool. But from the trailer it doesn't seem like either the story from the comic or a remake of the original movie, so it's baffling to me that they'd name this character Eric Draven. They should have just gone with a new character.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'll still check it out, but I'm not as excited for the movie as I was..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=djSKp_pwmOA\" data-code=\"djSKp_pwmOA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/djSKp_pwmOA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-17T11:49:19-07:00","id":1532774,"title":"","content":"I know that many movie remakes like the Crow or stuff based on lesser known heroes or villains like Kraven doesn\u2019t bode for the rest of the rest of 2024.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-17T19:29:10-07:00","id":1532792,"title":"","content":"I found newfound admiration for the Crow when I was in college; my high-school, friends, would go to the theater, twice or thrice a week to see it; they were big-time Brandon Lee fans. <br /> <br /> It was one of my first Requiem games I ran. Basically, the plot of the Crow, except one player is a vampire and his adversaries are mortals. I used a simple fantasy-map program to make the town and it was known as, Medieval Crow. He was embraced by the Vampire-Valkyrie and the Skull-Boy, a boy with a man-sized skull on his head, was his guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T02:39:21-07:00","id":1532802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1532766#post1532766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ohhh!! I saw the trailer for that Crow &quot;remake&quot; and whoa..... it does not look good. Well, if this was another Crow story about a different character, then I'd be more on board with it. When I first heard about it a few years back it was pitched as being closer to the story in the original comic rather than a remake of the movie, which I thought sounded pretty cool. But from the trailer it doesn't seem like either the story from the comic or a remake of the original movie, so it's baffling to me that they'd name this character Eric Draven. They should have just gone with a new character.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'll still check it out, but I'm not as excited for the movie as I was..</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't seen the Crow-Trailer before and... oh boy, that really does not look good. It's a remake of the Brandon Lee movie but also it gives off the vibes that it wants to be John Wick. And the writing... Man, I can already see the hallmarks of some typical stupid modern movie-writing (that movie-studios love so much) in that train-station-scene which seems to be some sort of supernatural dimension/land of the dead. You know because the one thing that original movie was missing was an entire scene where a character explains the whole movie to the protagonist... Crows carry souls, the main-character and his girlfriend are murdered and then he comes back from the dead for revenge. Done. No need to introduce some convoluted lore but that seems to be exactly what this movie is aiming to do... sigh<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T10:39:59-07:00","id":1532810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1532774#post1532774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that many movie remakes like the Crow or stuff based on lesser known heroes or villains like Kraven doesn\u2019t bode for the rest of the rest of 2024.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure there is some good stuff coming out, but those two movies in particular don't seem all that good. Maybe we'll be surprised though...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1532792#post1532792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found newfound admiration for the Crow when I was in college; my high-school, friends, would go to the theater, twice or thrice a week to see it; they were big-time Brandon Lee fans.<br /> <br /> It was one of my first Requiem games I ran. Basically, the plot of the Crow, except one player is a vampire and his adversaries are mortals. I used a simple fantasy-map program to make the town and it was known as, Medieval Crow. He was embraced by the Vampire-Valkyrie and the Skull-Boy, a boy with a man-sized skull on his head, was his guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh whoa! That sounds pretty cool! Thanks for sharing that! Glad that game went good for you...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1532802#post1532802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't seen the Crow-Trailer before and... oh boy, that really does not look good. It's a remake of the Brandon Lee movie but also it gives off the vibes that it wants to be John Wick. And the writing... Man, I can already see the hallmarks of some typical stupid modern movie-writing (that movie-studios love so much) in that train-station-scene which seems to be some sort of supernatural dimension/land of the dead. You know because the one thing that original movie was missing was an entire scene where a character explains the whole movie to the protagonist... Crows carry souls, the main-character and his girlfriend are murdered and then he comes back from the dead for revenge. Done. No need to introduce some convoluted lore but that seems to be exactly what this movie is aiming to do... sigh</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeeeaa..... it doesn't look great. And yea, having someone explain that concept to the main character does seem like an odd choice. I mean, the Crow TV series kind of did that, but at least it seemed better to me.<br /> <br /> But yea, for whatever reason this comes off as a supernatural actiony John Wick style flick and they reskinned it for The Crow. Which might not be a be a idea in and of itself, but them naming that character Eric Draven is really throwing me, as it makes no sense to call the character that and then him nothing like Eric from the either comics or the movie. Super weird...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T16:54:51-07:00","id":1532824,"title":"","content":"Personally I would have left the first Crow alone out of respect to the late Brandon Lee and Micheal Massri and made it somehow different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T01:45:16-07:00","id":1532838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1532810#post1532810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeeeaa..... it doesn't look great. And yea, having someone explain that concept to the main character does seem like an odd choice. I mean, the Crow TV series kind of did that, but at least it seemed better to me.<br /> <br /> But yea, for whatever reason this comes off as a supernatural actiony John Wick style flick and they reskinned it for The Crow. Which might not be a be a idea in and of itself, but them naming that character Eric Draven is really throwing me, as it makes no sense to call the character that and then him nothing like Eric from the either comics or the movie. Super weird...</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be that it's one of those where someone came up with an original movie and the movie-studio was like &quot;Only way we're gonna put this into production is if it's tied to an existing IP.&quot; and so the original script was rewritten to now be a Crow remake.<br /> <br /> Also, two other things stood out to me. The first one is that I wonder how well the action plays if the bit they're repeatedly doing in those action-scenes is that the protagonist literally cannot die. Not a lot of suspense left when the bad guys come after him with guns, knives and whatnot while the audience is fully aware that this will be completely useless against the undead guy. The second thing is it's a bit surprising how many shots we saw of the dead wife in the trailer. Neither the original Crow nor John Wick really delve that much into the dead wife character. That's of course because the movie is about the revenge so the dead wife is more a symbol than a character. It's more about what she represents than who she is. There was this moment of realization when I and my friends were going to watch John Wick 4 and I asked the round what John Wick's dead wife's name is and nobody knew (me included). But here the trailer hints at this movie having this whole sub-plot of her meeting the protagonist, falling in love and then her also stumbling upon the bad guy doing bad guy stuff. But I just can't picture that working. The inciting incident is the protagonist and his wife being murdered and the movie is about him taking revenge. And if they do it as flashbacks somehow, it comes off like just more exposition to explain what's going on. Even though the murder-part is more than enough to justify the revenge-part.<br /> <br /> And this trailer also made me think it's one of those where you pretty much get the whole movie already. What are the odds all the sequences in the opera house will be the literal finale of the movie? Yeah, not a good trailer... at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T16:53:37-07:00","id":1532876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1532824#post1532824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I would have left the first Crow alone out of respect to the late Brandon Lee and Micheal Massri and made it somehow different.</div> </div> </div> </div>My friends were outraged at the City of Angels. When I got the score to that movie, my friends refused to let me play it; I insisted because it was composed by Graeme Revell, and as far as I was concerned, it was a good score!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T11:28:40-07:00","id":1532912,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2521_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2521\" data-vbnamecard=\"2521\">Iguazu</a> I watched City of Angels and was pretty disappointed by the result and the only sequal was the one with Eric Mobius and Kristian Dunst that I had a soft spot for. Still the music for City Of Angels was decent to listen to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T16:51:38-07:00","id":1532927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1532838#post1532838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could be that it's one of those where someone came up with an original movie and the movie-studio was like &quot;Only way we're gonna put this into production is if it's tied to an existing IP.&quot; and so the original script was rewritten to now be a Crow remake.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's entirely possible. I know this remake has been in the works for many many years, but I wouldn't be shocked if they took something else and slapped The Crow label on it just to get something out the door.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1532838#post1532838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, two other things stood out to me. The first one is that I wonder how well the action plays if the bit they're repeatedly doing in those action-scenes is that the protagonist literally cannot die. Not a lot of suspense left when the bad guys come after him with guns, knives and whatnot while the audience is fully aware that this will be completely useless against the undead guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>They made it work in the original, but that was more Eric going after the guys one on one, there was only one big action scene where he took on a ton of dudes. We'll see how this plays I guess. I assume they're do the thing where the villain discovers he can steal his power or whatever...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1532838#post1532838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second thing is it's a bit surprising how many shots we saw of the dead wife in the trailer. Neither the original Crow nor John Wick really delve that much into the dead wife character. That's of course because the movie is about the revenge so the dead wife is more a symbol than a character. It's more about what she represents than who she is. There was this moment of realization when I and my friends were going to watch John Wick 4 and I asked the round what John Wick's dead wife's name is and nobody knew (me included). But here the trailer hints at this movie having this whole sub-plot of her meeting the protagonist, falling in love and then her also stumbling upon the bad guy doing bad guy stuff. But I just can't picture that working. The inciting incident is the protagonist and his wife being murdered and the movie is about him taking revenge. And if they do it as flashbacks somehow, it comes off like just more exposition to explain what's going on. Even though the murder-part is more than enough to justify the revenge-part.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I can't remember if they said the name of John Wicks wife in the original... surely they did.<br /> <br /> But yea, it definitely looks from the trailers like there will be a lot more with his wife. I suspect it'll be all flashback, but who knows. Maybe it'll just start with them meeting and getting into whatever kills them and then he comes back?<br /> <br /> The original comic did it as flash backs, and the movie did of course. Guess we'll see how it plays out..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1532838#post1532838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this trailer also made me think it's one of those where you pretty much get the whole movie already. What are the odds all the sequences in the opera house will be the literal finale of the movie? Yeah, not a good trailer... at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, that's the bad thing with trailers these days, they give way to much away. So yea, it does kinda seem like we've seen the whole thing already, but maybe there will still be some surprises... hopefully.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1532876#post1532876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My friends were outraged at the City of Angels. When I got the score to that movie, my friends refused to let me play it; I insisted because it was composed by Graeme Revell, and as far as I was concerned, it was a good score!</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually kinda liked City of Angels(Salvation too). I mean, it's not where near as good as the first one, but it's got some cool elements. I wish we could have maybe seen the directors original vision, but what we got wasn't too bad... least it wasn't as bad as Wicked Prayer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T17:48:15-07:00","id":1532930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1532927#post1532927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually kinda liked City of Angels(Salvation too). I mean, it's not where near as good as the first one, but it's got some cool elements. I wish we could have maybe seen the directors original vision, but what we got wasn't too bad... least it wasn't as bad as Wicked Prayer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I liked the atmosphere of City of Angels: And the City of Angels is my official name for LA in WoD RPG-games. I've never seen Salvation; I had to look up Wicked-Prayer; OMG, Edward Farlong as the Crow; that's worse than having Jon Bon Jovi as the Crow. And what are the Aztecs doing up in Arizona? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T04:09:22-07:00","id":1532938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1532930#post1532930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the atmosphere of City of Angels: And the City of Angels is my official name for LA in WoD RPG-games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's cool! Perfect name for an LA Chronicle.<br /> <br /> But yea, the look and feel of that movie is great! It's not a perfect movie my any means, but it's grown on me over the years..<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1532930#post1532930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never seen Salvation; I had to look up Wicked-Prayer; OMG, Edward Farlong as the Crow; that's worse than having Jon Bon Jovi as the Crow. And what are the Aztecs doing up in Arizona?</div> </div> </div> </div>Salvation isn't too bad actually. I mean, it's no where near as good as the original either, but it has it's moments. I think it's definitely worth a watch.<br /> <br /> Wicked Prayer though is awful. The book it's based on is really good though, but they somehow made it into the worst movie. And yea, Edward Furlong isn't great in it. There was a time when maybe he could he could have pulled it off, but it was not at the time of filming..<br /> <br /> There was a Crow tv series in the late 90's that was actually pretty good! It only went one season and ended on a cliffhanger (that I'm still pissed about), the show took the mythology in an interesting direction...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T17:58:28-07:00","id":1532975,"title":"","content":"Edward Furlong isn't a name that I haven't heard about in a long time and I know he was struggling with addictions and how it derailed a promising career.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T04:18:12-07:00","id":1532996,"title":"","c