,"value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T13:53:29-07:00","id":1533134,"title":"","content":"We all seen our share of awful movies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T04:16:42-07:00","id":1533162,"title":"","content":"Ok, just to change the subject quick, I just finished the apple tv series Silo and I thought it was great!! I haven't read the books it's based on, and I didn't know much about it, but I'm really glad I watched it! I thought I knew where the story might be going, but I was pretty surprised by the season 1 finale.<br /> <br /> So, I'll definitely be looking forward to season 2.<br /> <br /> I have a show on my list called Beacon 23 (which is on MGM+ I think) and II just found it also based on a book by the same author as the Silo series! So, I'll gotta watch that too! Hopefully it'll be as good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T12:00:31-07:00","id":1533177,"title":"","content":"I've read the first book of the Silo series and liked it, but I haven't gotten around to buying the second one of the series as I've been on a historical fiction and biography kick right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T12:05:22-07:00","id":1533181,"title":"","content":"Is Silo really that good? The premise seemed a tad dull to me. Weird place, authoritarian rules, weirdness just getting weirder, bad people get overthrown, turns out they had a reason to be bad and now the protagonist has to figure out what the alternative is... It just seemed like a formula, I've seen before... Snow Piercer, Wayward Pines, Lost... been there, done that. What exactly does Silo offer on that terrain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T12:11:46-07:00","id":1533183,"title":"","content":"I can only go by the book and not the tv show, but the one book was a good read and what possible society could happen in a post apocalyptic with humanity greatly reduced and the world is trashed and things we would take for granted would be seen as a luxury that can't be indulged. That type of idea always interested me when I first read the Stand by Stephen King and what scared wasn't the supernatural elements but the talk of Glen Bateman &amp; Stu Redman of what kind of society would likely form in a post plague world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T12:20:44-07:00","id":1533187,"title":"","content":"Okay, but does it do anything interesting with the formula...? At this point, a zombie-survival-story needs more than just a post-apocalyptic setting beset by zombies and having a bunch of humans trying to survive. The idea of a bunch of people being squashed into a place for mysterious reasons isn't that interesting on its own at this point. The Silo just doesn't seem that interesting. Snowpiercer certainly had a more intriguing premise, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T12:27:46-07:00","id":1533190,"title":"","content":"The second book explains why they had to hide out in the silos as it covers the events of a runaway technology that ran rampart over the planet and the leaders had to make some very tough choices and choose what they could tell to the citizens and especially when decades passed and they weren't certain how things were better. It's premise was in the same camp in the movie called The Colony starring Lawerence Fishburne and the late Bill Paxton where the few pockets of humanity are hiding underground from near total winter and the tough choices they had to make to keep there outposts alive as resources were few and even a common cold was a dangerous thing as it could spread to the rest of the group and they had to exile them or kill them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 03-27-2024, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T05:35:28-07:00","id":1533375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1533177#post1533177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read the first book of the Silo series and liked it, but I haven't gotten around to buying the second one of the series as I've been on a historical fiction and biography kick right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's cool! I liked the show so much I bought the books so I could read them. Not sure when I'll start em, but soon hopefully..<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1533181#post1533181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Silo really that good? The premise seemed a tad dull to me. Weird place, authoritarian rules, weirdness just getting weirder, bad people get overthrown, turns out they had a reason to be bad and now the protagonist has to figure out what the alternative is... It just seemed like a formula, I've seen before... Snow Piercer, Wayward Pines, Lost... been there, done that. What exactly does Silo offer on that terrain?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak to those other shows (though I did see the movie Snowpiercer), but Silo really sucked me in. The location is interesting, and there are some mysteries to the weird authoritarian rules. Plus the crux of the show resolves around a bit of a murder mystery that ties into the larger mysteries of the Silo. Maybe a bit of a spoiler, but the bad people don't get overthrown and we still don't totally know why they're bad. I really liked some of the world building too. Anyway, not sure what it was about it, but I really liked it. I got really drawn into it. Maybe it's the acting? It's got some great actors in it, and the lead Rebecca Ferguson is really good in this! I dunno... but I thought it was really well done and I'm definitely looking forward to the next season.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":24,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","user":"Mr Gone","date":". 03-30-2024, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T13:20:06-07:00","id":1533393,"title":"","content":"Finished watching an older film called American Heist with Adrian Brody, Hayden Christensian and Jordon Brewster and it's surprisingly good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;