yIOfc8SZEuJ9_GVj\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/g6oXeetkFu0?si=yIOfc8SZEuJ9_GVj\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/g6oXeetkFu0?si=yIOfc8SZEuJ9_GVj\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/g6oXeetkFu0?si=yIOfc8SZEuJ9_GVj </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T20:56:45-07:00","id":1533591,"title":"","content":"Finally was able to start reading the most recent Pendergast novel The Cabinet of Dr. Leng by Preston and Child, still having a time travel machine is pushing my suspension of disbelief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T05:37:06-07:00","id":1533691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1533584#post1533584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really a movie or a game, but I found this to good along with most of his other-works.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/g6oXeetkFu0?si=yIOfc8SZEuJ9_GVj\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/g6oXeetkFu0?si=yIOfc8SZEuJ9_GVj</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That was pretty interesting. Thanks for sharing!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1533591#post1533591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally was able to start reading the most recent Pendergast novel The Cabinet of Dr. Leng by Preston and Child, still having a time travel machine is pushing my suspension of disbelief.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never read any of those... they any good? And the new one is a time travel story?<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, forgot to say, after watching Silo I wanted the series Beacon 23(based on a book by the same person who wrote Silo) and it was pretty interesting. Season 2 starts soon, so I'll be looking forward to seeing more of that story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T07:13:18-07:00","id":1533696,"title":"","content":"I've watched the western TV-adaptation of The Three-Body Problem and surprisingly it's pretty good. Didn't expect them to keep the references to the Cultural Revolution from Cixin Liu's novel. But the one thing it really showed is that really good, solid Sci-Fi concepts alone can carry the show. The acting was fine, some good character-actors, some people from Game of Thrones but at the end of the day, it was still the Sci-Fi-story from Cixin Liu's book that was the most interesting part of the show.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1533375#post1533375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't speak to those other shows (though I did see the movie Snowpiercer), but Silo really sucked me in. The location is interesting, and there are some mysteries to the weird authoritarian rules. Plus the crux of the show resolves around a bit of a murder mystery that ties into the larger mysteries of the Silo. Maybe a bit of a spoiler, but the bad people don't get overthrown and we still don't totally know why they're bad. I really liked some of the world building too. Anyway, not sure what it was about it, but I really liked it. I got really drawn into it. Maybe it's the acting? It's got some great actors in it, and the lead Rebecca Ferguson is really good in this! I dunno... but I thought it was really well done and I'm definitely looking forward to the next season.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Then it goes on my watchlist<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T08:20:00-07:00","id":1533700,"title":"","content":"The series is pretty good Mr.Gone as it covers many of the strange cases of FBI agent Pendergast and some of his mates get involved in. They did make a movie on the first book called The Relic back in the 1990's but I don't remember if they had the agent in it for the film. Just think of it like the show Fringe so there was always a strangeness to the world he lives in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-06-2024, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T14:24:03-07:00","id":1533721,"title":"","content":"Saw a show from the '90's: Ray Bradbury theater, the Long Rain. The '50's story took place on Venus, before they knew what the planet was really made of. It takes place in a jungle with constant rain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T04:13:44-07:00","id":1533950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1533696#post1533696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've watched the western TV-adaptation of The Three-Body Problem and surprisingly it's pretty good. Didn't expect them to keep the references to the Cultural Revolution from Cixin Liu's novel. But the one thing it really showed is that really good, solid Sci-Fi concepts alone can carry the show. The acting was fine, some good character-actors, some people from Game of Thrones but at the end of the day, it was still the Sci-Fi-story from Cixin Liu's book that was the most interesting part of the show.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been wanting to watch it! Glad to hear it's pretty good. Hopefully I can start on it soon..<br /> <br /> \u200b <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1533696#post1533696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. Then it goes on my watchlist<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> I hope you like it! Let me know what you think when you get the chance to see it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1533700#post1533700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The series is pretty good Mr.Gone as it covers many of the strange cases of FBI agent Pendergast and some of his mates get involved in. They did make a movie on the first book called The Relic back in the 1990's but I don't remember if they had the agent in it for the film. Just think of it like the show Fringe so there was always a strangeness to the world he lives in.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Oh, that sounds pretty cool! I did like Fringe! Well, I might have to check it out sometime then. Thanks for the suggestion!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1533721#post1533721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saw a show from the '90's: Ray Bradbury theater, the Long Rain. The '50's story took place on Venus, before they knew what the planet was really made of. It takes place in a jungle with constant rain.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool! I might have to look into that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T11:10:14-07:00","id":1533982,"title":"","content":"I could add a little of X-files in there, but Pendergast is no Fox Mulder and isn't considered a joke, but the other agents find him unsettling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T04:08:47-07:00","id":1534020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1533982#post1533982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could add a little of X-files in there, but Pendergast is no Fox Mulder and isn't considered a joke, but the other agents find him unsettling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, ok! That's cool! Well, I'll have to add those books to my list! Thanks for the suggestion!<br /> <br /> Oh, totally off that subject, but I'm excited to see the Fallout TV series. I started playing Fallout 4 back in December. I'd never played any of the Fallout games and my kid suggested it. I just finished the main story on Monday and now I have a few of the DLCs left to finish. It's been pretty fun, so I'm looking forward to seeing what they do with the show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T06:47:16-07:00","id":1534023,"title":"","content":"<b>The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild 2)))</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28280-cappuchinapr","name":"cappuchinapr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T10:00:13-07:00","id":1534030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534020#post1534020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, totally off that subject, but I'm excited to see the Fallout TV series. I started playing Fallout 4 back in December. I'd never played any of the Fallout games and my kid suggested it. I just finished the main story on Monday and now I have a few of the DLCs left to finish. It's been pretty fun, so I'm looking forward to seeing what they do with the show.</div> </div> </div> </div>I played that one last year when there was a discount on Steam. In my playthrough, I joined the Underground Railroad and I did a stealth-build focused on VATS. It was fun, although I gotta say that I wasn't a huge fun of the whole base-building-stuff. But then again, I never vibed with that stuff. I never was interested in buying a house in the Elder Scrolls games either. And I'm generally not a fan of that kind of building like what you have in a lot of survival-games like Ark or more recently Palworld. From the DLC, I liked the Island-one the most. Really liked how that one resolved because of who I sided with.<br /> <br /> But you know what the craziest thing is? Now looking back on it... I liked my time with Fallout 4 far more than my time with Starfield.<br /> <br /> And I never tried Fallout 76. Although from other reactions I'm better off to not have spent time on that one.<br /> <br /> As for the TV-show, I think it's less the Fallout-aspect that has me excited but rather that Walton Goggins will play a major role in it. Justified Primeval was nice but it just reminded me that Walton Goggins was such an integral part of what made Justified a great show.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-12T15:07:49-07:00","id":1534109,"title":"","content":"Finally reading Eric H. Cline 1177 B.C. The Year Civilization Collapsed and it's quite interesting and you can see some parallels with what we are seeing today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T03:34:10-07:00","id":1534122,"title":"","content":"I saw Alex Garland's new movie Civil War and... it wasn't what I expected. It's a movie focused on photo-journalism in a warzone. The movie isn't really that interested in the worldbuilding, though, which felt a bit odd. There's a moment in the movie where Kirsten Dunst talks about how the job of photo-journalists is to just do the looking and thinking is someone else's job. And that's kinda the whole approach of the movie. The highlight of the movie was definitely the one scene where Jesse Plemons as a militia-guy appears. His performance was a hell of a scene-stealer. Overall, I liked this one more than Alex Garland's last one Men but I don't know, there's just something about the movie that kept me from really getting on its wavelength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T05:14:28-07:00","id":1534125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534030#post1534030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I played that one last year when there was a discount on Steam. In my playthrough, I joined the Underground Railroad and I did a stealth-build focused on VATS. It was fun, although I gotta say that I wasn't a huge fun of the whole base-building-stuff. But then again, I never vibed with that stuff. I never was interested in buying a house in the Elder Scrolls games either. And I'm generally not a fan of that kind of building like what you have in a lot of survival-games like Ark or more recently Palworld. From the DLC, I liked the Island-one the most. Really liked how that one resolved because of who I sided with.<br /> <br /> But you know what the craziest thing is? Now looking back on it... I liked my time with Fallout 4 far more than my time with Starfield.<br /> <br /> And I never tried Fallout 76. Although from other reactions I'm better off to not have spent time on that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh nice! Glad you had some fun with Fallout 4! I ended up siding with the Minutemen, as that seemed the most moral option, but I nearly joined the Railroad (and I'm still allied with them)! The Settlement building thing is ok, and I've helped the settlements, but it can be a little tedious sometimes. But I've enjoyed the game more than I thought I would. I like the VATS thing a lot, it's helped me out, since the aiming can be a bit wonky sometimes... at least for me.<br /> <br /> Maybe sometime I'll look into the other Fallout games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534030#post1534030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the TV-show, I think it's less the Fallout-aspect that has me excited but rather that Walton Goggins will play a major role in it. Justified Primeval was nice but it just reminded me that Walton Goggins was such an integral part of what made Justified a great show.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, Walton Goggins is great! I'm glad he's in this series!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534109#post1534109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally reading Eric H. Cline 1177 B.C. The Year Civilization Collapsed and it's quite interesting and you can see some parallels with what we are seeing today.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I've never read it. Maybe I'll add it to my list sometime..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534122#post1534122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw Alex Garland's new movie Civil War and... it wasn't what I expected. It's a movie focused on photo-journalism in a warzone. The movie isn't really that interested in the worldbuilding, though, which felt a bit odd. There's a moment in the movie where Kirsten Dunst talks about how the job of photo-journalists is to just do the looking and thinking is someone else's job. And that's kinda the whole approach of the movie. The highlight of the movie was definitely the one scene where Jesse Plemons as a militia-guy appears. His performance was a hell of a scene-stealer. Overall, I liked this one more than Alex Garland's last one Men but I don't know, there's just something about the movie that kept me from really getting on its wavelength.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I've heard a bit to that effect lately, that it wasn't quite like the trailers made it out to be. The trailer had a bit of a weird vibe too though, and I wondered how much they'd actually get into what exactly was going on in the world. Seems with something like you'd want to dig into what happened to cause the conflict and dig into the worldbuilding a bit.. but I guess that's what they decided to do.<br /> <br /> I might check it out sometime...I've liked some of the Alex Garlands other movies..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T10:08:27-07:00","id":1534138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534125#post1534125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh nice! Glad you had some fun with Fallout 4! I ended up siding with the Minutemen, as that seemed the most moral option, but I nearly joined the Railroad (and I'm still allied with them)! The Settlement building thing is ok, and I've helped the settlements, but it can be a little tedious sometimes. But I've enjoyed the game more than I thought I would. I like the VATS thing a lot, it's helped me out, since the aiming can be a bit wonky sometimes... at least for me.<br /> <br /> Maybe sometime I'll look into the other Fallout games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would recommend Fallout: New Vegas. That one isn't from Bethesda directly but instead was developed by Obsidian. They did the Pillars of Eternity games recently which were pretty good as well, not Baldurs Gate 3 good but as far as CRPGs go, pretty good. But Fallout New Vegas is the one I liked the most from the Fallout-series so far. I played 3, New Vegas and well, 4.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534125#post1534125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never read it. Maybe I'll add it to my list sometime...</div> </div> </div> </div>I've read it years ago and it's great. Definitely a recommend as far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534125#post1534125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, I've heard a bit to that effect lately, that it wasn't quite like the trailers made it out to be. The trailer had a bit of a weird vibe too though, and I wondered how much they'd actually get into what exactly was going on in the world. Seems with something like you'd want to dig into what happened to cause the conflict and dig into the worldbuilding a bit.. but I guess that's what they decided to do.<br /> <br /> I might check it out sometime...I've liked some of the Alex Garlands other movies...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really small and it isn't a spoiler because it's just one line that gets offhandedly mentioned... but at one point you get the exposition that the US-President in this movie's setting is a third-time-President (which would be illegal under current US-laws) that has disbanded the FBI and has used drones to bomb protestors within the US. It's just one line so that's really all you get. But there's other bizarre stuff as well like how it seems the faction that is going to take over are the so-called &quot;Western Forces&quot; which is this alliance between the state of Texas and the state of California.<br /> <br /> And I think I finally figured out what has been nagging me: The conceit of the movie is that you have these photo-journalists in New York and they hear the rumor that the Western Forces are pushing towards Washington DC and plan to encircle the city. It seems like the President's days are numbered. And so they decide to go on a road trip, to get to DC before the Western Forces do their thing, to interview the President before it's all over. And so what the movie is really like is that you follow these journalists on this road trip with these episodic adventures. But the whole reason that there's never much of an interaction between the journalists and the world around them is that they're <i>photo</i>-journalists. They're just there to take pictures of the whole thing. But the whole conceit of the movie is these guys aiming to have an interview with the President. There are moments where I thought &quot;Okay, you've taken the picture, now interview the guy. Let's hear what he thinks about the world he lives in.&quot; and that never happens. It's really this mindset I've mentioned before that they're just there to take pictures and thinking is someone else's job.<br /> <br /> I'm also just wondering... If this had been a movie about photo-journalists in a warzone of the past, like the Vietnam War or Operation Desert Storm in the 90s or the Iraq/Afghanistan wars of the War on Terror in the early 00s... Would this level of disinterest in world-building work? I feel like since it's about journalists you'd want to have them hit on some sort of truth about the conflict, and have them gain some sort of insight through their investigations (aka interviews, chasing rumors, taking pictures etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T13:11:09-07:00","id":1534144,"title":"","content":"It's a good book Mr. Gone and the writing isn't dry as I sometimes find when the cover such subjects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T01:29:39-07:00","id":1534231,"title":"","content":"I saw the Fallout TV show and it's <i>really </i>good. Not only do you have a great cast (not just Walton Goggins) but the series actually nails the vibe and the look of the games. And it's chockful of references to the games. The people who made this series seem to actually like the games and appreciate what they do. I know, it's insane. When you have shows like the Witcher or Halo where the creators are proud to tell you how little interest they have in adapting the source-material, it's great to have a show like Fallout that demonstrates that you can still do your own thing while also showing appreciation for the source-material. And I have to mention that the show looks great. From the power-armor to the Pip-boys to what the ruined landscape looks like. It's all really well-done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T11:24:41-07:00","id":1534259,"title":"","content":"It's sounds like Fallout as a tv series is good Knightingale, usually they do a poor job with adapting popular games in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T17:55:05-07:00","id":1534278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534138#post1534138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would recommend Fallout: New Vegas. That one isn't from Bethesda directly but instead was developed by Obsidian. They did the Pillars of Eternity games recently which were pretty good as well, not Baldurs Gate 3 good but as far as CRPGs go, pretty good. But Fallout New Vegas is the one I liked the most from the Fallout-series so far. I played 3, New Vegas and well, 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh cool, thanks for the suggestion. I think I'll add it to my list and try to play it soon!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534138#post1534138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really small and it isn't a spoiler because it's just one line that gets offhandedly mentioned... but at one point you get the exposition that the US-President in this movie's setting is a third-time-President (which would be illegal under current US-laws) that has disbanded the FBI and has used drones to bomb protestors within the US. It's just one line so that's really all you get. But there's other bizarre stuff as well like how it seems the faction that is going to take over are the so-called &quot;Western Forces&quot; which is this alliance between the state of Texas and the state of California.<br /> <br /> And I think I finally figured out what has been nagging me: The conceit of the movie is that you have these photo-journalists in New York and they hear the rumor that the Western Forces are pushing towards Washington DC and plan to encircle the city. It seems like the President's days are numbered. And so they decide to go on a road trip, to get to DC before the Western Forces do their thing, to interview the President before it's all over. And so what the movie is really like is that you follow these journalists on this road trip with these episodic adventures. But the whole reason that there's never much of an interaction between the journalists and the world around them is that they're <i>photo</i>-journalists. They're just there to take pictures of the whole thing. But the whole conceit of the movie is these guys aiming to have an interview with the President. There are moments where I thought &quot;Okay, you've taken the picture, now interview the guy. Let's hear what he thinks about the world he lives in.&quot; and that never happens. It's really this mindset I've mentioned before that they're just there to take pictures and thinking is someone else's job.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds... odd. I mean, in the case of going to interview the President, wouldn't at least one of them be a regular journalist or something?<br /> <br /> The whole thing kinda sounds like they filmmakers didn't want to take sides, so they wrote their characters so they didn't take sides. Ugh.. the whole things sounds kinda pointless. If you're not going to dig into the world a little bit with something like this then whats the point?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534138#post1534138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also just wondering... If this had been a movie about photo-journalists in a warzone of the past, like the Vietnam War or Operation Desert Storm in the 90s or the Iraq/Afghanistan wars of the War on Terror in the early 00s... Would this level of disinterest in world-building work? I feel like since it's about journalists you'd want to have them hit on some sort of truth about the conflict, and have them gain some sort of insight through their investigations (aka interviews, chasing rumors, taking pictures etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally with you! You'd think you'd want them to get some kind if insight into what was happening... maybe that's just us?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534144#post1534144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a good book Mr. Gone and the writing isn't dry as I sometimes find when the cover such subjects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, cool! Thanks for letting me know. I'll have to look into it.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534231#post1534231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw the Fallout TV show and it's <i>really </i>good. Not only do you have a great cast (not just Walton Goggins) but the series actually nails the vibe and the look of the games. And it's chockful of references to the games. The people who made this series seem to actually like the games and appreciate what they do. I know, it's insane. When you have shows like the Witcher or Halo where the creators are proud to tell you how little interest they have in adapting the source-material, it's great to have a show like Fallout that demonstrates that you can still do your own thing while also showing appreciation for the source-material. And I have to mention that the show looks great. From the power-armor to the Pip-boys to what the ruined landscape looks like. It's all really well-done.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm 3 episodes in so far and I absolutely love it! And yea, it seems like they really nailed the look and feel of the world. It's great! I'm glad the people involved seemed to really be on board with the games and wanting to make sure it was true to games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-16T05:17:17-07:00","id":1534293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534278#post1534278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds... odd. I mean, in the case of going to interview the President, wouldn't at least one of them be a regular journalist or something?<br /> <br /> The whole thing kinda sounds like they filmmakers didn't want to take sides, so they wrote their characters so they didn't take sides. Ugh.. the whole things sounds kinda pointless. If you're not going to dig into the world a little bit with something like this then whats the point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it sounds like that. They just didn't want to take sides. But even then... You don't necessarily have to wade into current-day political stuff, particularly culture wars and such. Even more general themes like &quot;power corrupts&quot; or something would suffice. Instead, it's all just vibes.<br /> <br /> That's the thing I've seen in positive reviews a lot. That it's just this general vibe of things being bad. And some seem to like it that way.<br /> <br /> I think one of them is supposed to be the regular journalist who'll do the interview. It's an older journalist by Stephen Henderson. The role is fine. But another big disappointment is the last third and how it all ends. Especially because the president is played by Nick Offerman and (without getting into spoilers) I feel like the movie doesn't make full use of having somebody like him in that role.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534278#post1534278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm 3 episodes in so far and I absolutely love it! And yea, it seems like they really nailed the look and feel of the world. It's great! I'm glad the people involved seemed to really be on board with the games and wanting to make sure it was true to games.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a great show. Also, this is such a good show that I don't think that having any experience with the games is necessary to enjoy the show. Reminds me of the Cyberpunk 2077 Anime which was so great (and which gave a huge boost to the Cyberpunk 2077 videogame after its lackluster launch).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T04:12:41-07:00","id":1534328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534293#post1534293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it sounds like that. They just didn't want to take sides. But even then... You don't necessarily have to wade into current-day political stuff, particularly culture wars and such. Even more general themes like &quot;power corrupts&quot; or something would suffice. Instead, it's all just vibes.<br /> <br /> That's the thing I've seen in positive reviews a lot. That it's just this general vibe of things being bad. And some seem to like it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, sounds like there is definitely a better way to handle it.<br /> <br /> There was a movie in the ate 90's called <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0120086/\" target=\"_blank\">The Second Civil War</a> that, while a comedy, dug into things a little bit and dealt with how the media spins things. It's not perfect or anything, but sounds like they at least tried to dig into things a bit more than this movie does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534293#post1534293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one of them is supposed to be the regular journalist who'll do the interview. It's an older journalist by Stephen Henderson. The role is fine. But another big disappointment is the last third and how it all ends. Especially because the president is played by Nick Offerman and (without getting into spoilers) I feel like the movie doesn't make full use of having somebody like him in that role.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, if you're gonna get Nick Offerman you should at least make good use of him. That's sad..<br /> <br /> But, I'll check it out sometime maybe. Sounds like it had potential that they ultimately didn't do much with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534293#post1534293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a great show. Also, this is such a good show that I don't think that having any experience with the games is necessary to enjoy the show. Reminds me of the Cyberpunk 2077 Anime which was so great (and which gave a huge boost to the Cyberpunk 2077 videogame after its lackluster launch).</div> </div> </div> </div>I finished Fallout last night and whoa! That last episode!!! Season 2 cannot get here fast enough!<br /> <br /> And I still gotta check out that Cyberpunk anime. I've heard good things, so I'm glad to hear you like it too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T13:19:00-07:00","id":1534367,"title":"","content":"This is an older movie, but I'm looking forward to watching Den Of Thieves with Geread 