2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T12:40:09-07:00","id":1534403,"title":"","content":"No I didn't Knightingale, but I do enjoy seeing Mr. Butler playing these type of characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T16:27:41-07:00","id":1534419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534367#post1534367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an older movie, but I'm looking forward to watching Den Of Thieves with Geread Butler and some other heist style movies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Been quite a while since I've seen that one! I might have to revisit it sometime. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T18:32:27-07:00","id":1534422,"title":"","content":"I seen that movie and Cop Shop with him and Frank Grillo and that was a fun movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T14:51:19-07:00","id":1534462,"title":"","content":"I saw &quot;The Ministry of Ungentlemanly Warfare&quot;, Guy Ritchie's newest movie and it was a lot of fun. Going into the movie with a beer was definitely a good idea. It's that kind of movie. Typical WWII-pastiche with action. There's nothing fanciful happening here. Henry Cavill was great as a kleptomaniac rogue as the leader of the mission. But the real standout was Alan Ritchson (he also plays Jack Reacher in the Reacher TV show) as a Swedish guy who loves to use bow and arrow in the action-scenes. The reason he's the standout is that the movie feels very much like it's traveling on rails (and that includes the characters... it's all very function-oriented). It's all very typical but why Alan Ritchson stands out is that there's a scene where it centers on him being gay and then he proceeds to explain who he would and wouldn't wanna date in the group and when the guy he would wanna date protests, he starts flirting with him. For a movie that is almost exclusively about action and plot, that scene stands out. I wish the other guys in the group had similar scenes that explored their characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T12:07:43-07:00","id":1534500,"title":"","content":"Started to watch Cyborg Glass Shadow that is an indirect follow up to the Jean Claude Van Damme film. It's pure guilty pleasure notable for having a very young Angelina Jolie, the late and legendary Jack Palance who shot this before he did City Slickers and Canadian actor Elias Koteas when he still had a full head of hair and the always fun to watch Billy Drago chewing up scenery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T04:18:39-07:00","id":1534582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534462#post1534462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw &quot;The Ministry of Ungentlemanly Warfare&quot;, Guy Ritchie's newest movie and it was a lot of fun. Going into the movie with a beer was definitely a good idea. It's that kind of movie. Typical WWII-pastiche with action. There's nothing fanciful happening here. Henry Cavill was great as a kleptomaniac rogue as the leader of the mission. But the real standout was Alan Ritchson (he also plays Jack Reacher in the Reacher TV show) as a Swedish guy who loves to use bow and arrow in the action-scenes. The reason he's the standout is that the movie feels very much like it's traveling on rails (and that includes the characters... it's all very function-oriented). It's all very typical but why Alan Ritchson stands out is that there's a scene where it centers on him being gay and then he proceeds to explain who he would and wouldn't wanna date in the group and when the guy he would wanna date protests, he starts flirting with him. For a movie that is almost exclusively about action and plot, that scene stands out. I wish the other guys in the group had similar scenes that explored their characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've only heard a little about this one, but it's all been good, so glad to hear you liked it too. Defiantly sounds like something I'd like, so I'll have to check it out!<br /> <br /> I'm a little surprised the other guys didn't have a stand out character building moment like Alan Ritchson though. But, the movie still sounds pretty fun, thanks for the review.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1534500#post1534500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Started to watch Cyborg Glass Shadow that is an indirect follow up to the Jean Claude Van Damme film. It's pure guilty pleasure notable for having a very young Angelina Jolie, the late and legendary Jack Palance who shot this before he did City Slickers and Canadian actor Elias Koteas when he still had a full head of hair and the always fun to watch Billy Drago chewing up scenery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have I not seen this movie!? I'll have to check that out!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I recently watched 'Late Night with the Devil' and thought it was pretty good. It's got a lot of hype right now, and I'm not totally sure it lives up to all of it, but it was still really good. The way the story unfolds is great and I was pretty surprised where it all went. I recommend it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>