for only which only one could win. Truthfully it's slightly better then the alien origin and that's not a high bar and it seems that only Michael Ironside was having fun and he did say in an interview that he knew it was going to be awful and just have fun with it and boy did he ever with his scenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-17-2024, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T11:57:49-07:00","id":1535658,"title":"","content":"Nothing cheers me up faster then watching a Space Ice video where he roasts a Steven Seagal movie and the one called Ticker was something as you wonder how the late Dennis Hopper, Tom Sizemore and a young Jamie Pressley got roped into doing such a film?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T20:23:42-07:00","id":1535839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1535465#post1535465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is totally in the wrong thread, but, I read in the back of V:tM how they recommended Highlander, but not Highlander II, and then I remembered, I think in an R.Talsorian's Interface Magazine, they said this about the sequel, &quot;Highlander II, the Sickening, There Should Have Been Only One&quot;. So I watched a few clips of Highlander 2; I did watch the movie, back in the mid-90's. I don't remember much; however, the clips I saw, were dark, very Cyberpunk, gothic, however, I know that it was filmed in Buenos Aires, right after the Falklands, so, the extras weren't happy about the British. It wasn't a terrible movie; I kind of like it because of the atmosphere and, I used to live in South America.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1535515#post1535515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind Iguazu about your topic. Speaking of which did you ever watch the Director's cut of Highlander 2 where they removed all mention of them being aliens and changed them to people from the ancient past that got exiled to the future for only which only one could win. Truthfully it's slightly better then the alien origin and that's not a high bar and it seems that only Michael Ironside was having fun and he did say in an interview that he knew it was going to be awful and just have fun with it and boy did he ever with his scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a loooooong time since I've seen either version of Highlander 2. Been a bit since I've seen the original Highlander too.... I might have to revisit those sometime soon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1535658#post1535658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing cheers me up faster then watching a Space Ice video where he roasts a Steven Seagal movie and the one called Ticker was something as you wonder how the late Dennis Hopper, Tom Sizemore and a young Jamie Pressley got roped into doing such a film?</div> </div> </div> </div>How have I not heard of that one before!? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Might have to check it out, just to see how bad it is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T11:51:58-07:00","id":1535860,"title":"","content":"To be fair Mr. Gone I think this movie was still at a point in his career where Seagal was still considerable as something bankable but his popularity was clearly on the wane and started to care less about making an effort at acting. Anyway I'm looking forward to reading a biography on Randy Macho Man Savage and a book on the great Persian Kings today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-18-2024, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T17:11:37-07:00","id":1535876,"title":"","content":"Reading a book about Gypsies; this is a very scholarly book and it contradicts with the WoD: Gypsies book from '94. But, if you're going to run a Gypsies game, I would suggest reading it. For CoD or NWoD, Gypsies can be simple psychics or the lot, or just anyone that's an outcast in Tudor-England and puts on some weird cloths and calls themselves an, &quot;Aegyptian&quot;. They started outs outcasts from the Medieval Feudal-system and appeared around 1400s. <br /> <br /> I am losing interest in reading the book; perhaps it's too scholarly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T12:06:35-07:00","id":1535914,"title":"","content":"So far the Persian history book on the great kings is interesting and holds my attention and makes me want to study more about there empire. I mean they were one the first superpowers in the classic ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T12:24:41-07:00","id":1535917,"title":"","content":"I've watched the X-Men 97 animated series and man... This is now the second time since Andor that Disney has surprised me. This series is the follow-up to the cartoon from the early 90s but for whatever reason the premise for this series is: Imagine the teens who grew up with this cartoon writing a <i>very </i>mature sequel to that series. Like with Andor, I'm surprised that Disney allowed this because all the rest of their Marvel/Star Wars stuff is nothing like this. Genocide, racism, PTSD, parenthood, disability... imagine all these themes, apply them to an X-Men cartoon - and then imagine writing that never pulls its punches (and that includes character-deaths). This is a series that actually succeeded in turning a comic-typical clone-storyline into some really good drama, for example.<br /> <br /> If you've been reading X-Men comics the last couple decades you probably can see the outlines of the storylines they're aiming for with some of the characters but the writing in this season was pretty good. So any follow-up is in good hands, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-20T04:29:07-07:00","id":1535982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1535917#post1535917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've watched the X-Men 97 animated series and man... This is now the second time since Andor that Disney has surprised me. This series is the follow-up to the cartoon from the early 90s but for whatever reason the premise for this series is: Imagine the teens who grew up with this cartoon writing a <i>very </i>mature sequel to that series. Like with Andor, I'm surprised that Disney allowed this because all the rest of their Marvel/Star Wars stuff is nothing like this. Genocide, racism, PTSD, parenthood, disability... imagine all these themes, apply them to an X-Men cartoon - and then imagine writing that never pulls its punches (and that includes character-deaths). This is a series that actually succeeded in turning a comic-typical clone-storyline into some really good drama, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely loved X-Men '97! I loved the original series too, and I was pretty excited when this series was announced. I was hoping it'd at least be as good as the original series, but they really outdid themselves with this one. They worked in lots of stuff from some of the older comic story lines, but made it their own thing while mixing in all the themes you mentioned (which were always a part of X-Men anyway). I'm glad this was so good and I'm really looking forward to where they go from here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1535917#post1535917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you've been reading X-Men comics the last couple decades you probably can see the outlines of the storylines they're aiming for with some of the characters but the writing in this season was pretty good. So any follow-up is in good hands, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sadly haven't read the comics in close to 20 years now, but I was a HUUUUGE X-Men fan and read/collected them for years. I still have all my old comics! But yea, they borrowed heavily from some of those old comic story lines and I think they did a great job at adapting them while doing something a little new.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-20T08:19:22-07:00","id":1535988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1535982#post1535982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I absolutely loved X-Men '97! I loved the original series too, and I was pretty excited when this series was announced. I was hoping it'd at least be as good as the original series, but they really outdid themselves with this one. They worked in lots of stuff from some of the older comic story lines, but made it their own thing while mixing in all the themes you mentioned (which were always a part of X-Men anyway). I'm glad this was so good and I'm really looking forward to where they go from here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely wanted to watch it because as a kid I watched the X-Men cartoons but after watching Ahsoka and that latest season from Mandelorian, I wasn't too enthused about what this would be like. Seemed like an obvious nostalgia-cashgrab. So I had low expectations but man, not only did it exceed my expectations but it's a genuinely good show. Even stuff like Xavier and the cosmic Marvel side of things... Would never have expected them to stay faithful to that part as well!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1535982#post1535982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sadly haven't read the comics in close to 20 years now, but I was a HUUUUGE X-Men fan and read/collected them for years. I still have all my old comics! But yea, they borrowed heavily from some of those old comic story lines and I think they did a great job at adapting them while doing something a little new.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would highly recommend Jonathan Hickman's run on X-Men about Krakoa (starting in 2019, I believe). Really a highlight of the last couple of years for me. In that run, he takes the idea of a Mutant nation to a whole other level.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-20T19:32:49-07:00","id":1536027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1535914#post1535914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far the Persian history book on the great kings is interesting and holds my attention and makes me want to study more about there empire. I mean they were one the first superpowers in the classic ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a book I recently (a few months ago), at a library; I don't remember the name, but it was mostly about the Persian rulers and a little about their society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T11:38:05-07:00","id":1536069,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't doubt it as the book I'm reading does focus on it's kings and also focus on how they were able to create an effective infastructure to stay in power for a many centuries until Alexander The Great beat them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T05:43:58-07:00","id":1536247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1535988#post1535988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely wanted to watch it because as a kid I watched the X-Men cartoons but after watching Ahsoka and that latest season from Mandelorian, I wasn't too enthused about what this would be like. Seemed like an obvious nostalgia-cashgrab. So I had low expectations but man, not only did it exceed my expectations but it's a genuinely good show. Even stuff like Xavier and the cosmic Marvel side of things... Would never have expected them to stay faithful to that part as well!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I'm really glad they stuck so close to the feel of the original series and comics, while still doing a bit of their own thing. I wasn't really sure what to expect going in, but it really blew me away. They packed in so much to each episode and dealt with some pretty mature themes, much like the comics, which was really nice to see.<br /> <br /> Can't wait to see what they do next season!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1535988#post1535988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would highly recommend Jonathan Hickman's run on X-Men about Krakoa (starting in 2019, I believe). Really a highlight of the last couple of years for me. In that run, he takes the idea of a Mutant nation to a whole other level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh cool! Thanks for the suggestion. I'll try to check that out sometime!<br /> <br /> I'm trying to remember what I even read last... maybe the first part of X-Men: The End? I want to say I read some of Avengers vs X-Men, but can't quite remember... Anyway, I'm super behind. LOL.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Totally unrelated to all of this, I wanted the movie 'Boy Kills World' last night and thought it was pretty good! The action was pretty cool, and it's got a decent enough story to string it all along. H. Jon Benjamin does the voice over for the main character and it's great! If you haven't heard of it, check it out. It was pretty fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T11:18:53-07:00","id":1536265,"title":"","content":"The X-Men cartoon along with the Batman Animated series was must see viewing for me in the early 1990's and they are still excellent viewing to this day. On a different note I saw the trailer for the Furiso prequel and it looks good and it has George Miller still at the helm but I have mixed feeling about it not having Mad Max in it and more about fleshing out her backstory and Immortan Joe's rise to power. I get the Star Wars Prequel vibes about it as it we really don't need a backstory at all and part of the fun of the Mad Max series was making educated guesses about the character's back stories and seeing what we agreed upon. All said I'll probably check it out when it's on streaming services or DVD/Blu-Ray.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T18:08:39-07:00","id":1536322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1536069#post1536069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't doubt it as the book I'm reading does focus on it's kings and also focus on how they were able to create an effective infastructure to stay in power for a many centuries until Alexander The Great beat them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to look at the book the next time I had to the library; (it's only 0.5 miles away from me!). I've been interested in Persia since, well, it appeared on a random name-generated program I downloaded in the late-90's called, Every Changing Book of Names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T18:16:39-07:00","id":1536323,"title":"","content":"Also, speaking of libraries, I picked up, <i>The Last Duel, Kandahar </i>and<i> John Wick. </i>Hope they're good!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T05:36:23-07:00","id":1536342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1536265#post1536265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The X-Men cartoon along with the Batman Animated series was must see viewing for me in the early 1990's and they are still excellent viewing to this day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally! They're both still awesome! And I was surprised that new X-Men ''97 was as good as it was!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1536265#post1536265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a different note I saw the trailer for the Furiso prequel and it looks good and it has George Miller still at the helm but I have mixed feeling about it not having Mad Max in it and more about fleshing out her backstory and Immortan Joe's rise to power. I get the Star Wars Prequel vibes about it as it we really don't need a backstory at all and part of the fun of the Mad Max series was making educated guesses about the character's back stories and seeing what we agreed upon. All said I'll probably check it out when it's on streaming services or DVD/Blu-Ray.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I'm not totally sure we needed that backstory, but from everything I hear the movie is awesome, so I'm looking forward to seeing it. Furisoa was a pretty great character, so I'll be looking forward to see what they do with her backstory in this..<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T12:22:09-07:00","id":1536376,"title":"","content":"I would love to see one more Mad Max film with Mel Gibson in it, but alas he feels that he is way to old for the role and the audience wouldn't be down with it. I think he could still pull off an older bad ass Mad Max.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T12:23:12-07:00","id":1536377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1536322#post1536322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll have to look at the book the next time I had to the library; (it's only 0.5 miles away from me!). I've been interested in Persia since, well, it appeared on a random name-generated program I downloaded in the late-90's called, Every Changing Book of Names.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny enough it was the Palladium sourcebook Pantheons of the Megaverse that got me interested in other pantheons from the world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T04:51:31-07:00","id":1536417,"title":"","content":"So, I've seen Furiosa and it was good. A fun action-movie. I don't think it really made a good case for why we needed this prequel and it isn't nearly as good as Fury Road but on its own terms it's good fun. The action is still good, although the movie clearly relied on more CGI this time around. One thing I really didn't expect was for how long you'd see kid-Furiosa in this movie and it's only at the midway-point where it transitions to Anya Taylor-Joy. I think her performance is good and once she makes that final transformation to where she looks like in Fury Road, she actually manages to do a decent Charlize Theron impression. Of course, it also helps that she doesn't have to say a whole lot. Chris Hemsworth as Dementus is also good, I think. He's doing the &quot;funny Thor&quot;-thing but with more psychopath-vibes. Furiosa has this relationship with Tom Burke who plays this driver who had Furiosa's position as main-driver before her. And that part's a bit weird. They're close but it's very understated. In fact, it's so understated, it's hard to tell whether they're in love or just good friends or it's a mentor-student-connection... And it doesn't get a lot of screen-time either, so that makes it even harder to pinpoint what exactly was going on there.<br /> <br /> But the standout for me was the costume-design and the character-work in the movie. You of course already have this striking imagery with Imorten Joe and the War Boys. But Dementus has this band of misfits and there are like five or six very distinct henchmen who just ooze personality (both in looks and performance). The movie absolutely nails that part. Like, the doctor in the group calls himself &quot;the Organic Mechanic&quot;. Just a lot of creative ideas on display there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T12:02:49-07:00","id":1536449,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you like it Knightingale and I will check Furiosa out on streaming or when it comes out on DVD &amp; Blu Ray and make my own judgements about it and all already I'm leaning towards giving it a chance just because it has George Miller still behind the helm and alsoI'm seeing the old garbage comments that are popping up on social media again when Fury Road came out and they made such awful comments when it came out but this time it's more sexist in tone. Your not really helping your case on why you don't like the film at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T23:00:23-07:00","id":1536483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1536417#post1536417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've seen Furiosa and it was good. A fun action-movie. I don't think it really made a good case for why we needed this prequel and it isn't nearly as good as Fury Road but on its own terms it's good fun. The action is still good, although the movie clearly relied on more CGI this time around. One thing I really didn't expect was for how long you'd see kid-Furiosa in this movie and it's only at the midway-point where it transitions to Anya Taylor-Joy. I think her performance is good and once she makes that final transformation to where she looks like in Fury Road, she actually manages to do a decent Charlize Theron impression. Of course, it also helps that she doesn't have to say a whole lot. Chris Hemsworth as Dementus is also good, I think. He's doing the &quot;funny Thor&quot;-thing but with more psychopath-vibes. Furiosa has this relationship with Tom Burke who plays this driver who had Furiosa's position as main-driver before her. And that part's a bit weird. They're close but it's very understated. In fact, it's so understated, it's hard to tell whether they're in love or just good friends or it's a mentor-student-connection... And it doesn't get a lot of screen-time either, so that makes it even harder to pinpoint what exactly was going on there.<br /> <br /> But the standout for me was the costume-design and the character-work in the movie. You of course already have this striking imagery with Imorten Joe and the War Boys. But Dementus has this band of misfits and there are like five or six very distinct henchmen who just ooze personality (both in looks and performance). The movie absolutely nails that part. Like, the doctor in the group calls himself &quot;the Organic Mechanic&quot;. Just a lot of creative ideas on display there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I just got back from seeing it. I agree that the surprising thing for me was the side characters. They all had personality and were memorable, even if they were just around for a few moments. And yeah, fantastic movie that didn't need to get made. It wasn't as good as Fury Road, but Fury Road was really, really really good. This one was just really good. I came away without any real complaints. I'm glad I caught it in theaters, I was gonna skip and wait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T04:23:49-07:00","id":1536494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1536376#post1536376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love to see one more Mad Max film with Mel Gibson in it, but alas he feels that he is way to old for the role and the audience wouldn't be down with it. I think he could still pull off an older bad ass Mad Max.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might just be me, I'm good with Gibson not returning to the role. I liked Tom Hardy as Max, but I think it'd be interesting to let other play the part and really give it that &quot;Legend&quot; vibe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1536417#post1536417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've seen Furiosa and it was good. A fun action-movie. I don't think it really made a good case for why we needed this prequel and it isn't nearly as good as Fury Road but on its own terms it's good fun. The action is still good, although the movie clearly relied on more CGI this time around. One thing I really didn't expect was for how long you'd see kid-Furiosa in this movie and it's only at the midway-point where it transitions to Anya Taylor-Joy. I think her performance is good and once she makes that final transformation to where she looks like in Fury Road, she actually manages to do a decent Charlize Theron impression. Of course, it also helps that she doesn't have to say a whole lot. Chris Hemsworth as Dementus is also good, I think. He's doing the &quot;funny Thor&quot;-thing but with more psychopath-vibes. Furiosa has this relationship with Tom Burke who plays this driver who had Furiosa's position as main-driver before her. And that part's a bit weird. They're close but it's very understated. In fact, it's so understated, it's hard to tell whether they're in love or just good friends or it's a mentor-student-connection... And it doesn't get a lot of screen-time either, so that makes it even harder to pinpoint what exactly was going on there.<br /> <br /> But the standout for me was the costume-design and the character-work in the movie. You of course already have this striking imagery with Imorten Joe and the War Boys. But Dementus has this band of misfits and there are like five or six very distinct henchmen who just ooze personality (both in looks and performance). The movie absolutely nails that part. Like, the doctor in the group calls himself &quot;the Organic Mechanic&quot;. Just a lot of creative ideas on display there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the review! Glad to hear you liked it! I was wondering how long we'd see kid Furisoa, so that's interesting it's a pretty significant amount. Though I'm glad Anya Taylor-Joy does a good job in the role too! And if Chris Hemsworth brings in a little of the 'Bad Times at the El Royale' vibe, then it should be good! Oh, and glad all the little side characters get a little fleshed out, that's always nice!<br /> <br /> Well, I'm really looking forward to seeing it!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1536483#post1536483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I just got back from seeing it. I agree that the surprising thing for me was the side characters. They all had personality and were memorable, even if they were just around for a few moments. And yeah, fantastic movie that didn't need to get made. It wasn't as good as Fury Road, but Fury Road was really, really really good. This one was just really good. I came away without any real complaints. I'm glad I caught it in theaters, I was gonna skip and wait.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear you liked it too!<br /> <br /> It's nice to hear that even though it might not needed to have been made, that it was still enjoyable. (I felt the same about Solo, I don't think it was needed but I enjoyed it more than expected.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T12:07:57-07:00","id":1536517,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Mr Gone;n1536494]<br /> <br /> Might just be me, I'm good with Gibson not returning to the role. I liked Tom Hardy as Max, but I think it'd be interesting to let other play the part and really give it that &quot;Legend&quot; vibe.<br /> <br /> <br /> Fair enough and I greatly enjoyed Tom Hardy doing the role and wouldn't mind seeing him do it again and I was more then willing to give him a chance as both George Miller and Mel Gibson both thought he would be great in the role. But while I disagree with Mel Gibson thinking that he is to old for the role and think that he can pull it off still, we have to respect his choice and he felt the same way when he was offered the Russell Crowe in Gladitor and said more or less &quot;don't you think that I'm getting to old for these type of roles?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T05:38:15-07:00","id":1536668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1536517#post1536517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough and I greatly enjoyed Tom Hardy doing the role and wouldn't mind seeing him do it again and I was more then willing to give him a chance as both George Miller and Mel Gibson both thought he would be great in the role. But while I disagree with Mel Gibson thinking that he is to old for the role and think that he can pull it off still, we have to respect his choice and he felt the same way when he was offered the Russell Crowe in Gladitor and said more or less &quot;don't you think that I'm getting to old for these type of roles?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I don't always think people are too old to return to roles, it mostly depends on the story they want to tell with the character. Like Harrison Ford with Indiana Jones. The latest movie was about him being old, so it works for him to come back.<br /> <br /> So, they could maybe do a movie with Mel Gibson about an old Mad Max. But, those movies have always seemed to be more about the myth or legend of Max, so I think it'd be interesting to have slightly different versions of the character played by different actors. It could be cool..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, in slightly different news, I recently watched 'The Fall Guy' with Ryan Gosling and Emily Blunt and it was great! I went in not expecting much but it was really fun!! I definitely recommend it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T12:04:11-07:00","id":1536675,"title":"","content":"Fall Guy I remember the tv series that it was based on and I may check it out when it comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T12:19:05-07:00","id":1536680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1536323#post1536323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, speaking of libraries, I picked up, <i>The Last Duel, Kandahar </i>and<i> John Wick. </i>Hope they're good!</div> </div> </div> </div>John Wick is certainly a fun movie to watch and a nod to the laconic protagisnt who actions speak louder then mere words ever could. On a totally different note I've been watching Dark Side Of Ring that deals with the tragic behind the scenes stories of professional wrestling. The ones on Owen Hart and Brian Pillman were especially tragic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 06-01-2024, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T12:57:12-07:00","id":1536681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1536675#post1536675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fall Guy I remember the tv series that it was based on and I may check it out when it comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only vaguely remember the TV show. I'm sure the movie isn't very much like it, but there are a few nods to the show...<br /> <br /> It was a fun movie though. Ryan Gosling and Emily Blunt were great in it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T09:08:52-07:00","id":1536699,"title":"","content":"I only have vague memories of it myself and watched it from time to time on a retro tv channel that would play shows like that and that how I was introduced to Columbo, McCloud, Six Million Dollar Man and other shows from 1970's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T08:26:07-07:00","id":1536747,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, I liked Fall Guy as well. A nice mix of rom-com and action.<br /> <br /> I also saw Kingdom of the Planet of the Apes recently. It struck a bit of a different tone compared to the previous ones. It starts with a big time-jump where we are many generations in the future after Caesar has died. The movie is trying to be more of an adventure (with some really obvious story-beats, though...). Noa, the main-character belongs to this tribe of apes who are into falconry but then he witnesses his tribe getting abducted to the titular kingdom. And there he has to deal with this ape-king who believes it's time to reclaim humanity's legacy. Since he's the bad guy he obviously is talking about human weaponry, of course. And Noa saw his dad die during the abduction and since then his father's eagle has been following him but attacks him whenever he comes close... You can see from a mile away how this all is gonna play out. But it was fun enough... until the last 20 minutes. Man, that part really soured me on the movie. Because what I didn't know when I went into this movie is that this is supposed to be the start of a trilogy. So that ending part is throwing a lot of stuff at the wall with little pay-off - because what it's doing instead is setting up the next movie. That was disappointing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T10:50:41-07:00","id":1536755,"title":"","content":"I don't think that 2024 isn't going to be a good year for Hollywood in general as more people watching more indie films or from smaller studios that can't afford all bells and whistles that Disney, Warner Bros or Universal Studios can do and focus on telling good enjoyable stories with the budget and audience they have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T16:49:33-07:00","id":1536820,"title":"","content":"I'm really getting into Sarah J. Maas Glass of Thrones and her Crescent City series and how good she is at world building.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avat