m":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T00:26:29-07:00","id":1537063,"title":"","content":"Let's not give Disney ideas to ruin IP's even more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T04:55:12-07:00","id":1537076,"title":"","content":"I've played Star Trek Resurgence from Dramatic Labs and it was great. A friend had recommended it to me as he's a fan of Star Trek. And yeah, this game nails the tone of Star Trek. It's like a Telltale game with a lot of dialogue-choices and this whole &quot;This character will remember this&quot;-dynamic. But I was surprised by how much more gameplay this game had compared to your usual Telltale game. Some of it felt a bit like tedium, like having to scan multiple things. Sometimes it felt more like busywork than gameplay. But other than that, it was nice to not just do quicktime-events with button-presses all the time. And they actually got Jonathan Frakes to voice Riker for the game. Also, Piotr Michael does a really good Leonard Nimoy impression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T07:50:45-07:00","id":1537082,"title":"","content":"Ever since Enterprise went off the air all those years ago, I gradually lost interest in the series and I heard that the most recent fare isn't all that great and doesn't feel like classic Trek at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T13:05:39-07:00","id":1537104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1537082#post1537082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ever since Enterprise went off the air all those years ago, I gradually lost interest in the series and I heard that the most recent fare isn't all that great and doesn't feel like classic Trek at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't believe I have done it... but I've seen all five seasons of Star Trek Discovery. Man, the one thing I can say about the show is that they were always going for some wild swings with their narrative. In the end, the visuals were great and the performances as well. Tig Notaro as chief engineer was great. And all the performers were great, really. It's just... the writing. If anything, Sonequa Martin-Green who played the main-character of this show... She started in the first season as a human who was raised by Vulcans and somehow was also that little sister of Spock that nobody has ever heard about. Fast forward to the fifth season and you have a completely different character. But not because of character-growth. The characterization was very inconsistent and felt more like the writers trying to do course corrections throughout these five seasons. You didn't miss a lot with this one.<br /> <br /> The first two seasons of Picard were a mess as well. I thought the third season was fun, though. Because they finally remember that all the audience wants is for Patrick Stewart and Jonathan Frakes to have a fun adventure. And you can watch that one on its own, I think. Really, if you were to ask me about any of these references to previous seasons of Picard, my answer would just be &quot;You don't wanna know...&quot;.<br /> <br /> Star Trek Strange New Worlds is fun, though. It goes for a more episodic format and it has served that show really well so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T13:32:19-07:00","id":1537111,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m watching the film Baby Driver with Jamie Foxx and Kevin Spacey and whatever issues Mr. Spacey has in his personal life he is one talented actor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T13:38:40-07:00","id":1537114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1537111#post1537111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m watching the film Baby Driver with Jamie Foxx and Kevin Spacey and whatever issues Mr. Spacey has in his personal life he is one talented actor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked that one. Not as good as the Cornetto-trilogy but still pretty fun. Have you seen &quot;Last Night In Soho&quot;? That has been Edgar Wright's latest. I think that was the first one of his movies that I didn't have a great time with.<br /> <br /> Also, as for alternate universes... I really would've liked to see the version of Ant-Man that was directed by Edgar Wright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d"