ore/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T20:00:19-07:00","id":1537129,"title":"","content":"Black Mass was a good movie and I read at least two true crime books on James &quot;Whitey&quot; Buglar and his death also raised questions of why he wasn't put in solitary confinement when it was discovered that he was working with the FBI for years as a informant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T04:27:25-07:00","id":1537298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1537116#post1537116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have seen Last Night In Soho with Matt Smith and Anne Taylor Joy and enjoyed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I watched that a bit back ago and thought it was really good! I didn't know much about it going in (other than who directed it) and I was pleasantly surprised by it! I had no idea where it was all going, but I highly enjoyed it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T01:09:26-07:00","id":1537469,"title":"","content":"Hmm, maybe I should give Last Night In Soho another chance then. I saw it when it released and it didn't really grab me.<br /> <br /> But I saw two movies recently that I did really like. The first is Richard Linklater's newest movie called Hitman starring Glen Powell and Adria Arjona. The closest thing you could compare this to are Coen Brothers movies: a dark comedy revolving around crime. But it's only kinda like that. The premise is that Glen Powell plays this philosophy-teacher who helps the local police-department with setting up sting-operations for catching people who try to hire hitmen. One day the undercover-cop who usually talks to the target is suspended for using excessive force in some other context. And so the Glen Powell character takes over instead - and he's good at it. This role is a godsent for any actor because he's essentially playing a character who loves acting because he changes his appearance and style every time he meets with a target depending on what they expect a hitman to be like. But the plot really only kicks in when at one time the target is a woman who wants him to kill her abusive husband. And so what he does instead this time is to talk her out of hiring him - because he's fallen in love with her. The movie's real fun and what also makes it work is that Glen Powell and Adria Arjano have great chemistry. I also was looking up Adria Arjano because she looked familiar and upon looking it up... she was one of the actors in Morbius <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />... Well, at least she's in a good movie this time around.<br /> <br /> The other movie might be my favorite movie of the year so far for me: It's called &quot;I Saw The TV Glow&quot;. This is the second movie from Jane Schoenbrun I've seen. I wasn't the biggest fan of We're All Going To The World's Fair but it certainly was an interesting film. This new one I liked a lot more. It's about two teenagers, Owen and Maddy, who bond over being fans of the same TV show called The Pink Opaque which is this mix between Buffy The Vampire Slayer and Twin Peaks. It's about two sisters fighting against monsters. Then the show gets cancelled and they both drift apart. Years later Maddy approaches Owen again and tells him that she has found a way to travel into the show and inhibit the body of one of the sisters and she wants him to take over the other sister so that they can continue their adventures as depicted in the show. There's a lot more going on than that and it doesn't go where you might think it does. I looked it up on Wikipedia and there they call it a &quot;psychological horror-drama&quot;. I guess that kinda describes it. But I loved it! One's relationship to media, life expectations, gender and sexuality... it all kinda comes up in the movie. There's a lot going on. Definitely worth a watch!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T12:40:01-07:00","id":1537572,"title":"","content":"I just watched Blind War with lots of gun fu with Andy On.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T13:03:54-07:00","id":1537578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1537469#post1537469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I saw two movies recently that I did really like. The first is Richard Linklater's newest movie called Hitman starring Glen Powell and Adria Arjona. The closest thing you could compare this to are Coen Brothers movies: a dark comedy revolving around crime. But it's only kinda like that. The premise is that Glen Powell plays this philosophy-teacher who helps the local police-department with setting up sting-operations for catching people who try to hire hitmen. One day the undercover-cop who usually talks to the target is suspended for using excessive force in some other context. And so the Glen Powell character takes over instead - and he's good at it. This role is a godsent for any actor because he's essentially playing a character who loves acting because he changes his appearance and style every time he meets with a target depending on what they expect a hitman to be like. But the plot really only kicks in when at one time the target is a woman who wants him to kill her abusive husband. And so what he does instead this time is to talk her out of hiring him - because he's fallen in love with her. The movie's real fun and what also makes it work is that Glen Powell and Adria Arjano have great chemistry. I also was looking up Adria Arjano because she looked familiar and upon looking it up... she was one of the actors in Morbius <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />... Well, at least she's in a good movie this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>That one is on my list to watch! Glad to hear you liked it.. I was wondering how it was. Sounds like it should be pretty fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1537469#post1537469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other movie might be my favorite movie of the year so far for me: It's called &quot;I Saw The TV Glow&quot;. This is the second movie from Jane Schoenbrun I've seen. I wasn't the biggest fan of We're All Going To The World's Fair but it certainly was an interesting film. This new one I liked a lot more. It's about two teenagers, Owen and Maddy, who bond over being fans of the same TV show called The Pink Opaque which is this mix between Buffy The Vampire Slayer and Twin Peaks. It's about two sisters fighting against monsters. Then the show gets cancelled and they both drift apart. Years later Maddy approaches Owen again and tells him that she has found a way to travel into the show and inhibit the body of one of the sisters and she wants him to take over the other sister so that they can continue their adventures as depicted in the show. There's a lot more going on than that and it doesn't go where you might think it does. I looked it up on Wikipedia and there they call it a &quot;psychological horror-drama&quot;. I guess that kinda describes it. But I loved it! One's relationship to media, life expectations, gender and sexuality... it all kinda comes up in the movie. There's a lot going on. Definitely worth a watch!</div> </div> </div> </div>I watched it Friday and I'm not sure what I think about it. I did some reading online afterwards about what it's an allegory for, and I think I can get that meaning. It was well made and looked awesome. Everyone in it is really good too, but I'm just not sure what I think about it all together, especially with the way it ended. I'm not sure how I expected it to end I guess, but it seemed a little lacking maybe? I'm still thinking about it so I guess that counts for something.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it was still worth watching and I'm glad I saw it...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr