<div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1537999#post1537999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Picked up Robert Kirkman's Transformers the other day and I did enjoy it and the team did make nods to original G1 lore such as Skyfire and Starscream being friends before the war, Spike's Dad working at a oil refinery and having one of the Seekers being the first to come back online by Teletran 1.<br /> <br /> Kirkman is already tying Transformers with GI-JOE as we have Duke in a small role and in general creating a shared universe under the Energon line</div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool they're crossing over Transformers and G.I. Joe! Have they tried to do that before? And didn't they make a mention of it one of the new Transformers movies?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think that's a pretty cool idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I need to make some time to read some comics again. I haven't read any in a looooong time. I still have my collection, but I haven't gotten anything new in quite a while...<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, totally aside, I watched Furoisa last week and loved it!! I thought it fit in nicely with Fury Road without trying to be the exact same movie. I thought the backstory was pretty interesting and Anya Taylor-Joy did a great job playing that character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> ________________________________