07:00","id":1538100,"title":"","content":"I'm curious when Robert Kirkman does his Cobra Commander story if they're nods to the Marvel Comics series where we learn the why's of the path he took and if they will include him having a son and him having ties to Zartan and Snake Eyes and Storm Shadow or will they take a different path?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T20:51:02-07:00","id":1538223,"title":"","content":"I glanced through the GI-JOE Duke book and they did have some nods to the Marvel Comics series such as the PITT and it's was nice to see characters like Scrap Iron, Major Bludd and some of the lesser known Cobras as well as seeing Destro, Flint, Lady Jaye, The Baroness getting some screen time and seeing the Baroness working with Duke. I wonder how the Cobra Commander story will be like and if he will be as ruthless and skilled as he was in the Marvel Comics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T01:27:29-07:00","id":1538228,"title":"","content":"I saw Beverly Hills Cop: Axel F this weekend and surprisingly it was pretty good. It's one of those nostalgia-sequels with Eddy Murphy reprising his role as an older Axel F who's helping out his daughter (who's a defense attorney) and there are a lot of cameos and references from the first three movies. But it's a fast-paced Action-comedy that holds up. For one, the characters they bring back are still the same great character-actors they were before with people like Paul Reiser, Judge Reinhold and John Ashton reprising their roles. And the new cast is good as well. Joseph Gordon-Levitt as a younger detective is pretty good. Taylor Paige as Eddy Murphy's daughter is okay but that's more because the whole plot is a bogstandard paint-by-numbers affair. She doesn't get to do a whole lot. The movie's exactly what you think it is. But it's fun for what it is.<br /> <br /> The MVP on the cast is definitely Kevin Bacon, though. He plays the sleazy corrupt cop villain in the movie and man, he nails that role. If anything, they should've given him more scenes. Because he takes that archetypical character and really elevates it with his performance. He brings the right energy to that character to make him so much more compelling than what he's like in the script.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T11:25:55-07:00","id":1538242,"title":"","content":"Kevin Bacon has a knack for playing sleazy cops or scummy people in general. Interestingly enough Eddie Murphy has wanted to do a sequel for Beverly Hills Cop, but the scripts he would get weren't age appropriate as he felt that it wouldn't do to pretend that his character wouldn't be older and have a family at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-08-2024, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T20:36:37-07:00","id":1538281,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it so does actor Mickey Rourke that he has a affinity for slimy characters himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T12:14:57-07:00","id":1538310,"title":"","content":"I think one thing that's interesting about Beverly Hills Cop is that it started as a Sylvester Stallone vehicle. Then due to some disagreements and creative differences, Sylvester Stallone left and while completely rethinking the movie, they got Eddie Murphy as the new lead and a more comedy-focused script. Meanwhile, Sylvester Stallone released his preferred version as well which then would be called Cobra. I saw that one again during the Christmas days last year... I don't know, didn't have a great time with the movie that time around. Stallone's performance felt stilted and too &quot;try-hard&quot;-y/forced. But it's interesting how Eddie Murphy starring in the first Beverly Hills Cop was a bit of a coincidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T13:59:56-07:00","id":1538320,"title":"","content":"That's an interesting tidbit about Stallone being considered as Axel Foley and I'm glad that they went with Eddie Murphy as I can't see Mr. Stallone pulling off the comedic elements of the film. Speaking of Cobra and how bad film was, the actor Brian Thompson who played the baddie said in an interview of how he struggled to understand what the reasons for his character's actions and what was the cult's end goal or motivation and was never given a good answer at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T15:25:56-07:00","id":1538395,"title":"","content":"I saw Abigail a vampire movie today and found it a fun popcorn \ud83c\udf7f film.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T04:49:39-07:00","id":1538418,"title":"","content":"Yesterday I saw Kill, directed by Nikhil Nagesh Bhat. It's this Indian action-movie that's a mix between John Wick and Die Hard (but on a train). This is the premise (from Wikipedia): &quot;When army commando Amrit finds out his girlfriend Tulika is engaged against her will, he boards a New Delhi-bound train in a daring quest to derail the arranged marriage. But when a gang of knife-wielding thieves led by the ruthless Fani begins to terrorize innocent passengers on the train, Amrit takes on the thieves in a death-defying spree to save those around him - turning what should have been a typical commute into an adrenaline-fueled thrill ride.&quot;<br /> <br /> The reason I saw it is that I had heard of the John Wick producers already planning an English remake of this movie. And once I saw it, I can kinda see why. The plot and the characters are all pretty formulaic but what absolutely stands out is the great fight choreography and the use of practical blood-effects. The action is absolutely brutal. And there's a turn in terms of plot in the middle of the movie that surprised me. I had not expected this movie to have the guts to go there. I still think I liked it less than movies like Raid: Redemption or John Wick but it was definitely a fun watch.<br /> <br /> But now I'm wondering how they're going to handle a remake of this because there are two important parts to this movie: One, a lack of guns and two, the societal context of India.<br /> <br /> _________________________________<br /> <br /> I saw Abigail a while ago. That was a good horror-movie. I especially liked Dan Stevens' performance in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T10:53:33-07:00","id":1538436,"title":"","content":"Dan Stevens performance was good and so was the young girl who played Abigail and a pretty good depiction of a lower humanity elder who likes to play with there food.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T06:35:55-07:00","id":1538650,"title":"","content":"I saw Longlegs yesterday and it was way better than I expected. It stars Maika Monroe as an FBI agent who's part of a manhunt for a serial killer. It's a very slow-paced movie but it makes up for that by excelling in atmospheric storytelling. The direction, the soundtrack, Maika Monroe's performance... This is one of those horror-movies that's all about vibes. Nicholas Cage is the serial killer but he has way fewer scenes in the movie than you might think with his name above the title. But man, it's a great performance. When he's there on the screen, he's nailing it in terms of creepiness. I can't think of a past performance I would compare it to. But that's typical for Nicholas Cage, I guess. You can always bet on him making interesting choices with his performance (both for good and ill depending on the movie in question <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> I'm still wrestling with myself whether I like the ending or not. I certainly didn't expect the movie to go there and the explanation also went further than I thought. It's like the ending offered too much information and not enough at the same time. I know, that's contradictory but it's like I either would've liked it to be more ambiguous or offer even more of a conclusive ending.<br /> <br /> But it's a good movie. I definitely gonna watch this one again when it gets its streaming-release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T14:18:03-07:00","id":1538676,"title":"","content":"Nicolas Cage has stated that he plans on cutting back making movies in the near future and Longlegs could be the start of him taking a well earned break.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T07:50:10-07:00","id":1538838,"title":"","content":"Well, that wouldn't be surprising. For many years he had to do all these B-movies because of his money-troubles and now that he's kinda back and managed to crawl out of that financial hole, I guess he feels like he earned himself a little break <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T16:22:39-07:00","id":1538876,"title":"","content":"I recently watched Alex Garland's Civil War movie. It was fine and wasn't as bad as I expected. Though, I wish we had a little more info about what caused the conflict and how the factions divided up. There's a few vague references, but I think it'd help to get a little more backstory, just to at least get a little more info as to what each sides motivation was.<br /> <br /> Anyway, not a bad movie, but not all that great either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T14:15:43-07:00","id":1538919,"title":"","content":"Yes Cage did get into considerable debt and had to do all those B films to pay off the IRS and now he is good with them and kept on doing these type of films as they were fun and kept him out of trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T14:23:58-07:00","id":1538921,"title":"","content":"Now I'm watching a somewhat older film by Taratino called Resivor Dogs with Harvey Kitel, Michael Madsen, Tim Roth and lots of good character actors and actresses and seeing how some of them make mention of people they knew or worked with such as Mr. White knowing and working with Alablama from True Romance or that Mr. Blonde could be the brother of the hit man from Pulp Fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T14:37:03-07:00","id":1538924,"title":"","content":"Just recently watched The Dark Side Of The Ring special on late wrestler Chris Kaynon and that was a heartbreaking story of how he battled mental illness and struggling with his sexuality during a time when it would have ruined his career and his friends like Dallas Page, Chris Jericho and even Raven didn't know until much later and that his friend James Mitchel was a saint to putting up with Chris's manic bursts. I don't think many people could handle that rollercoaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T16:39:42-07:00","id":1539065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1538921#post1538921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm watching a somewhat older film by Taratino called Resivor Dogs with Harvey Kitel, Michael Madsen, Tim Roth and lots of good character actors and actresses and seeing how some of them make mention of people they knew or worked with such as Mr. White knowing and working with Alablama from True Romance or that Mr. Blonde could be the brother of the hit man from Pulp Fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great movie!! And yea, all the little connections that Tarantino sprinkles in are great. Well, I guess it could be said that other movies included references back to this, but still. It's cool he makes those connections..<br /> <br /> I rewatched Pulp Fiction weekend before last, and that's a great one too!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T18:17:02-07:00","id":1539070,"title":"","content":"Pulp Fiction was a good film and made me like Qeuntin style of films.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-24-2024, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T10:07:08-07:00","id":1539222,"title":"","content":"I saw &quot;Deadpool and Wolverine&quot; and I had a good time. There were the usual meta-commentary and humor you'd expect. And I was surprised a few times by where the movie went with its jokes. But I gott say: It makes fun of Marvel relying on the multiverse, cameos and references and the MCU being &quot;in a slump&quot;... except that also perfectly describes what this movie is doing. I think, though, that this one's better at it than other recent movies in the MCU. But I wonder what it would be like to watch this movie without understanding all the references it's using. And sometimes, it's really just... &quot;Hey, look who we brought back, guys!&quot;. <br /> <br /> Like I said, I had a great time during the movie, chuckled a few times - but afterwards... The more I thought about the movie on my way home, the less I cared about it. Not in a bad way or a good way. It's just more of a bit of ambivalence. Looking at the movie in retrospect, everything just felt slight, like there's not a lot going on beneath the surface. It's a fun movie but there isn't a whole lot of depth to it. MCU movies often aren't but between the referential meta-humor and the multiverse-stuff, it just enhances the feeling of it all feeling a bit superficial even more.<br /> <br /> If you're a fan of the MCU, it's worth going but otherwise... I don't think you're missing out on much by just waiting for the streaming-release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T15:39:19-07:00","id":1539256,"title":"","content":"I'm glad that you liked the new Deadpool movie and I'll probably wait for it to come on demand or streaming-release, but one movie I'm looking forward to is Alienoid which is a cool martial arts science fiction action film from Asia. I also plan on getting around to watching Sleeping Dogs with Russel Crowe who plays a Detective with memory problems and trying to recall a case that he isn't sure it was done properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-25-2024, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T04:27:48-07:00","id":1539307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1539222#post1539222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw &quot;Deadpool and Wolverine&quot; and I had a good time. There were the usual meta-commentary and humor you'd expect. And I was surprised a few times by where the movie went with its jokes. But I gott say: It makes fun of Marvel relying on the multiverse, cameos and references and the MCU being &quot;in a slump&quot;... except that also perfectly describes what this movie is doing. I think, though, that this one's better at it than other recent movies in the MCU. But I wonder what it would be like to watch this movie without understanding all the references it's using. And sometimes, it's really just... &quot;Hey, look who we brought back, guys!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I had a great time during the movie, chuckled a few times - but afterwards... The more I thought about the movie on my way home, the less I cared about it. Not in a bad way or a good way. It's just more of a bit of ambivalence. Looking at the movie in retrospect, everything just felt slight, like there's not a lot going on beneath the surface. It's a fun movie but there isn't a whole lot of depth to it. MCU movies often aren't but between the referential meta-humor and the multiverse-stuff, it just enhances the feeling of it all feeling a bit superficial even more.<br /> <br /> If you're a fan of the MCU, it's worth going but otherwise... I don't think you're missing out on much by just waiting for the streaming-release.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the review! I had a feeling it'd at least be fun.. and it sounds like it is. I've enjoyed all the other Deadpool movies, so I have no doubt I'll enjoy this one too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I had a feeling they might overdo it a bit with the cameos and such, but, I still think it'll be fun.<br /> <br /> Glad to hear you liked for the most part though, even if there isn't much depth to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1539256#post1539256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad that you liked the new Deadpool movie and I'll probably wait for it to come on demand or streaming-release, but one movie I'm looking forward to is Alienoid which is a cool martial arts science fiction action film from Asia. I also plan on getting around to watching Sleeping Dogs with Russel Crowe who plays a Detective with memory problems and trying to recall a case that he isn't sure it was done properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't heard about Alienoid or Sleeping Dogs, I'll have to look into those..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T14:23:32-07:00","id":1539440,"title":"","content":"They are lower budget films from lesser known studio, but Don't let that get in the way as they can make very good films with what they have to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T16:34:57-07:00","id":1539447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1539440#post1539440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are lower budget films from lesser known studio, but Don't let that get in the way as they can make very good films with what they have to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know how it goes. There are some great low budget movies out there! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\"