 can do the jobs well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh totally! It's nice to see some seasoned actors who are still awesome! And it's nice to see some of them interact with newcomers sometimes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T14:10:37-07:00","id":1539605,"title":"","content":"Glanced through Robert Kirkman's Cobra Commander and it was decent and they did have a few nods to the old material such as secretly taking over a town as his base of operations and how he recruited Destro to his team. I didn't care for them bringing in Cobra-La that Cobra Commander spent some of his time living there as a group bio-tech extremists didn't really fit inhmo and detracted from the lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T05:42:28-07:00","id":1539787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1539605#post1539605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glanced through Robert Kirkman's Cobra Commander and it was decent and they did have a few nods to the old material such as secretly taking over a town as his base of operations and how he recruited Destro to his team. I didn't care for them bringing in Cobra-La that Cobra Commander spent some of his time living there as a group bio-tech extremists didn't really fit inhmo and detracted from the lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear it's not too bad. I might have to check out some of the newer G.I. Joe based stuff. I haven't really read an G.I. Joe in a looooooong time. I think the last thing G.I. Joe related I even watched was maybe Retaliation? And the animated series Resolute?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, on to movies, I watched MaXXXine last night and thought it was really good! I liked X and Pearl, so I was pretty sure I'd like this too. It might be actually be better than the other ones? Maybe.. But, I enjoyed it! It's got a nice 80's vibe to it, and mixes in some Hollywood movie making with some satanic panic with a dash of slasher movie. It was pretty fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"