ter versions from IDW. I do like origins on how Orion Pax becomes Optimus Prime and Megatron starting off as a well intended rebel and becoming the very thing he fought against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T22:55:31-07:00","id":1543398,"title":"","content":"I decided to check out Longlegs the most recent Nicolas Cage film. Just like Acardia he has a much smaller role and makes the most of the screen time he has and him playing a disturbed person is old school for him and the make up job does a good job in adding to the creepy factor. It's going to be a sad day when he stops making movies on a regular basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T04:24:57-07:00","id":1543413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1543398#post1543398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I decided to check out Longlegs the most recent Nicolas Cage film. Just like Acardia he has a much smaller role and makes the most of the screen time he has and him playing a disturbed person is old school for him and the make up job does a good job in adding to the creepy factor. It's going to be a sad day when he stops making movies on a regular basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I watched Longlegs a few weeks back and highly enjoyed it. I didn't know much going in other than Nic Cage was in it, and I was pretty surprised by it! Nic Cage is super creepy in it!<br /> <br /> I also watched Cuckoo recently, I heard some buzz about it, and I thought it was pretty good too. Dan Stevens is great (as usual) in it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T06:28:42-07:00","id":1543419,"title":"","content":"I watched Longlegs when it came out and liked it. Especially the creepy vibe of the whole thing worked really well, I think. And looking back on it, I think that's why I liked the first half a bit more than the second half, especially towards the end when things coalesce and it's explained what's going on.<br /> <br /> I also saw Joker 2 recently... Sadly like many other people, I didn't like that one. Although the friends I was liked it even less than me, they absolutely hated it. Mostly because they were completely unaware that Joker 2 would have musical elements.<br /> <br /> But a recent movie I quite enjoyed was Stranger Darling. Directed and written by JT Mollner, it's a serial killer movie but it has a good/clever script. You will notice that immediately because the title says &quot;Stranger Darling: A tale told in six chapters&quot; and then it starts with chapter 3. But what really sold the movie for me was Willa Fitzgerald's performance. It's a very tricky role and she nailed it. I definitely would recommend that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T22:14:18-07:00","id":1543492,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to reading The Olympian Affair by Jim Butcher that has some great Steampunk vibes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T04:15:21-07:00","id":1543514,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, that one had come out last year. It's sitting somewhere on my bookshelf. I never ended up reading it because it was the follow-up to Aeronaut's Windlass which came out in 2015. So it's been ages since I read that first book... Therefore I wanted to re-read that first one again before digging into the second book. But then I never did... That and at the time when Aeronaut's Windlass came out, I remember liking that one less than Chris Wooding's Tales of the Ketty Jay series (it's pretty much Pirates of the Caribbean but with steampunk flavor).<br /> <br /> A book I'm looking forward to reading is Absolution from Jeff Vandermeer, the fourth book in his Southern Reach series. Really loved the trilogy (and the movie from Alex Garland).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T09:39:15-07:00","id":1543528,"title":"","content":"I picked up the previous book last year and waited patiently for it come out on softcover and paperback. So my memories of the novel is still somewhat fresh in my mind, but I know that I should reread the previous book to fill in the gaps and Steampunk and Cyberpunk or Cattlepunk are good genres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T14:32:05-07:00","id":1543543,"title":"","content":"John Grisham has written a sequel to The Firm, and in this case I have to reread the Firm to remember what kind of trouble that the Tom Cruise character got into when he made that deal with some scary people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T08:45:24-08:00","id":1545470,"title":"","content":"I saw two movies that I liked recently:<br /> <br /> The first one is Conclave, directed by Edward Berger. He did that recent &quot;All quiet on the western front&quot; WWI movie. It was... okay. I wasn't the biggest fan but I know some people really liked that one. Conclave is a mystery-thriller about the election of the new pope. And what makes it work is that it has this nice airport-book kind of pacing where you got a central mystery, a lot of twists and turns and things just keep moving. It's very pulpy in that regard. And to be honest the movie ended up being far more idealistic than I had expected. But the thing that elevates it is its cast. Ralph Fiennes, Stanley Tucci, John Lithgow... and the rest of the cast. All great actors and this movie wouldn't work without them. There's a lot of talking and a very limited cast so this movie heavily relies on the actors making this work - but they succeed. Really loved this one.<br /> <br /> I also saw Clint Eastwood's newest movie Juror Nr. 2. You definitely notice that it's a Clint Eastwood film with some decisions he made... like making the most prejudicious, gung-ho members in the jury the two black people in the room. And Toni Collette plays a prosecutor who's running for office but every time people talk about her becoming a politician, there's so much condescension in the word. Stuff like &quot;You used to be a lawyer, now you're a... <i>'politician'</i>.&quot; That's obviously Clint's direction at work there ( lol ). But there's some great direction as well. The essential trolley-problem is that the central character, a nice family man, accidentally ran over a woman at night in pouring rain. He didn't see that he hit her and her body was flung into a gorge and in the darkness he didn't see her. So he just drove off. But the reason she left the bar was because she was in a fight with her boyfriend. A boyfriend who's a criminal and who has been to prison before. So he gets blamed for the death. And at some point, the main-character talks himself into thinking that maybe the boyfriend should just go to prison. He's a criminal after all. But then the movie does this great thing where the main-character tries to make the case for this and Nicholas Hoult sells this well because he sounds so cowardly and desperate while arguing his case. I would recommend that one as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T08:47:03-08:00","id":1545471,"title":"","content":"Clint Eastwood knows his craft extremely well and he learned from some of the best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T08:57:15-08:00","id":1545472,"title":"","content":"The only thing that sucks is that Warner Bros has no interest in the movie - at all. Even though this could be Clint Eastwood's last film. Warner Bros is taking the movie out of theaters early and puts it on streaming (<a href=\"https://screenrant.com/juror-no-2-clint-eastwood-streaming-release-report-detail/\" target=\"_blank\">source</a>). Another case of David Zaslav's disastrous management... They already managed to push away Christopher Nolan and if Clint were younger, he would probably leave Warner Bros too after the way this movie was treated. Zaslav is running that movie-studio into the ground...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T09:19:16-08:00","id":1545476,"title":"","content":"That does suck that both Nolan and Eastwood got treated this way. They both have forgotten more about movie making then Zaslav would ever learn. It's harder and harder to find empathy for Hollywood studios that give self inflicted wounds like that and just recently Disney had to disclose that they had a pediafile working in there animation department for decades and he was on the sex offenders list in France and Disney didn't do there due diligence when they hired him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 11-06-2024, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T17:22:35-08:00","id":1546613,"title":"","content":"I recently picked up Transformers volume 2 by Robert Kirkman and it's still a good read and some minor spoliers.<br /> <br /> Starscream leadership of the Deceptions is over as he got overthrown by a pissed off Soundwave and shows that he is not just a pretty face and has solid leadership skills and has a vision that Starscream lacks.<br /> <br /> Shockwave is in the series, but sometime during the war he has gained a cruel and sadastic streak and many of his fellow Deceptions find him really distrubing and wouldn't be broken up if he died and didn't come back.<br /> <br /> Thundercracker and Astrotrain seem to feel sorry for the humans and find no pleasure of fighting us. Astrotrain in particular seems to feel sorry what will happen to Spike Witwicky when Shockwave gets his hands on him.<br /> <br /> Megatron is still missing in action, but if you read Cobra Commander then you know what has become of there leader.<br /> <br /> The countless eons of war have taken a toll on both sides and even they seem tired of the battle and want it to end.<br /> <br /> Now I'm looking forward to Destro and Scarlett from GI-Joe spot light. In particular I hope that the Destro issue will be good as I liked his portrayal in the old Marvel Comics. Maybe we can see ones on Zartan and Firefly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-08T18:47:09-08:00","id":1546780,"title":"","content":"I'm still waiting for the library to have a copy of <i>Godzilla: Minus One </i>available. I remember, when ID4 came out on VHS, I think it was around Thanksgiving-time, '96, I was so excited and