bcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1558476#post1558476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Age of Wonders; I have all the graphics to the first one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just one more day to go!<br /> <br /> Provided no unfortunate setbacks occur, the new AoW DLC drops tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-09T17:21:50-07:00","id":1558761,"title":"","content":"Finally, I found a book about daily life in Russia during the 16th century (actually, it's the 17th, but that's as close as I'm gonna get). Most libraries, only have books about the Soviet-Union in regards to Russia just like, all the German-history is just NAZIs. <br /> <br /> <i>Moscow and the Roots of Russian Culture</i> 1964: it's at a small, university's library. <br /> <br /> I'm also reading <i>Peoples and Cultures of the Middle East </i>2001: for a vampire game, based off of Salam Rushidie's works (kinda). No, it's not for <i>Requiem </i>but <i>Cyberpunk's Night's Edge</i>, because, I want to use modern-military action and CP2020 does a better job; so, it's basically a Middle-Eastern country ruled by a 1,000 year old vampire. Takes place in the 60's/50's/40's ish, and she's been ruling for decades. Anyways, the book is from an anthropological-perspective and it's a nice read. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1558727#post1558727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just one more day to go!<br /> <br /> Provided no unfortunate setbacks occur, the new AoW DLC drops tomorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, TBH, I don't think I've ever actually played AoW; just used the graphics for D&amp;D games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T08:19:27-07:00","id":1558792,"title":"","content":"The only Age of Wonders I didn't play was AoW 2. Not because I wasn't interested, but because I literally did not know it existed, until I heard AoW 3 was being worked on.<br /> <br /> General opinion also seems to be that AoW 2 and its expansion, Shadow Magic is the best in the series.","signat