6T05:28:16-07:00","id":1562180,"title":"","content":"I watched that new Masters of the Universe movie this weekend.It wasn't too bad. They got all the character designs down, and the story was pretty good. It didn't take itself too seriously either. If this movie could have been made when I was a kid playing with the toys, I'd probably have through it was the greatest movie ever made. LOL! I'm not sure how many kids would be into it these days though..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-26T10:10:37-07:00","id":1562189,"title":"","content":"Good question Mr. Gone about how many children would be into He-Man and The Masters of the Universe today. I know that the toys here are still on the shelves, but that can be a matter of cost as toys are not cheap..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-26T12:58:20-07:00","id":1562192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1562189#post1562189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good question Mr. Gone about how many children would be into He-Man and The Masters of the Universe today. I know that the toys here are still on the shelves, but that can be a matter of cost as toys are not cheap..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, toys these days seem pretty expensive. Though admittedly I haven't been down a toy isle in quite a while now..<br /> <br /> The movie itself was pretty fun though, so maybe some kids will watch the movie and then be interested in the toys? Who knows..<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-26T15:28:57-07:00","id":1562196,"title":"","content":"I can only speak for myself, but the Masters of the Universe toys are not selling out and I'm sure that some of it does with price and maybe lack of interest. It might be different at other places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-26T18:32:17-07:00","id":1562213,"title":"","content":"I've heard the movie bombed in theaters, but got momentum in streaming. People want to watch, but at home.<br /> <br /> How that's going for sales is hard to tell, but my 2 cents: Masters of the Universe is always selling, it has a solid demand. If the retailers ordered too much, what you're seeing may not be toys getting dust in the isles, but to big inventory that's still selling at a normal pace, so they keep replacing and filling the isles.<br /> <br /> As an exercise, let's say retailers expected to triple their sells but got a 10% increase instead. One that usually sells 10 action figures a week is now selling 11, but bought 30. Plenty to keep the isle looking new for some time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-26T19:08:24-07:00","id":1562215,"title":"","content":"Myself I usually don't go by box office results as we have seen movies that didn't do well in the box office are considered great films today. Off the top of my head we had John Carpenter The Thing, Blade Runner, Shawshank Redemption and recently Transformers 1 not doing well box office wise and people thought they were superior to what made money that point in time.<br /> <br /> If I enjoyed the movie and that to me is more than enough and worth the money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T09:47:22-07:00","id":1562262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1562215#post1562215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Myself I usually don't go by box office results as we have seen movies that didn't do well in the box office are considered great films today.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just analyzing the possible causes of the toys apparently tanking. Not analyzing the movie itself.<br /> <br /> Finances and economy is an area I work in and like, so this kind of stuff is interesting by itself to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T10:19:31-07:00","id":1562263,"title":"","content":"As I recall the tail end of the Pog craze and the first release of Star Wars action figures in years suffocated the toy market in the mid 90's. I remember that the Megaman cartoon show, which was actually quite popular in ratings, was cancelled due to lack of toy movement at that time.<br /> <br /> I'm not aware of any crazes or recent releases that could be having that effect now, but I don't exactly have my finger on the pulse of the toy market.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T16:43:30-07:00","id":1562285,"title":"","content":"True Montparnasse that some of the toy products can tank because of cost and how well they been out together. Some toys based off of popular franchises were ugly looking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T01:46:20-07:00","id":1562291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1562263#post1562263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall the tail end of the Pog craze and the first release of Star Wars action figures in years suffocated the toy market in the mid 90's. I remember that the Megaman cartoon show, which was actually quite popular in ratings, was cancelled due to lack of toy movement at that time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, upon retrospect, I realized I had a lot of toy collections as a kid.<br /> <br /> Ninja Turtles.<br /> <br /> G. I. Joes.<br /> <br /> Dragon Ball Z<br /> <br /> Aliens<br /> <br /> Spiderman<br /> <br /> Beanie Babies<br /> <br /> Gundam<br /> <br /> Transformers<br /> <br /> Hotwheels","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 07-29-2026, 04:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T02:08:17-07:00","id":1562292,"title":"","content":"For me my toy collections were the following <br /> <br /> Transformers <br /> GI-Joe <br /> Masters of the Universe <br /> Super Friends \ud83d\ude02","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T03:23:13-07:00","id":1562294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481606-any-good-movies-games-or-books-you-are-looking-forward-to?p=1562285#post1562285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True Montparnasse that some of the toy products can tank because of cost and how well they been out together. Some toys based off of popular franchises were ugly looking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Masters of the Universe is an ongoing toy line. It isn't as much based in the franchise as the other way around.<br /> <br /> Some collectors did complain about quality, but we're talking hardcore collectors of the line.<br /> <br /> I know what can happen, but I'm trying to figure out what did happen, and for now the problem seems to be distribution and excess expectations more than the toys tanking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T13:56:44-07:00","id":1562749,"title":"","content":"Finally saw the trailer for the new Divinity game by Larian Studios.<br /> <br /> It looked disgusting, but in a good way! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-18T20:21:05-07:00","id":1564171,"title":"","content":"I have recently become aware of the existence of a game called Vampire Syndicate, which is a tactical RPG that combines elements of Vampire: the Masquerade with X-Com, and is set in a Cyberpunk world. As the game is still in early access, it's very bare bones right now; but from what's been talked about so far, it shows a ton of promise.<br /> <br /> The basic premise to the game so far, is that you start off as a mortal working the streets of Moonfall, who hires themselves as a mercenary to one of four possible lineages of vampires. As you continue to do missions for them and build your reputation, you steadily climb up the ranks, eventually being granted the privilege of becoming one of them. It's also implied that in future updates, we may be able to seize control of the lineage as its new leader, and force our rivals out of the city.<br /> <br /> What makes the vampires stand out from each other, is that they aren't just divergent bloodlines. Each of the different lineages exist as their own totally separate species, who's powers and physiology are unique to their particular lineage. Even the manner in which they reproduce is different.<br /> <br /> <br /> The lineage which I'm currently most interested in are the <b>Cthonians</b>, who have a Lovecraftian theme to them. They claim that their origins are linked back to some kind of eldritch being, whom they worship like a god, and are trying to find a way to bring about their return to our world.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another lineage are the <b>Sunseekers</b>, who's progenitor was cursed with vampirism after slaying an Egyptian snake goddess and being splattered in its blood. She originally created her lineage as a knightly order to protect mortals from supernatural threats, but they have since fallen from this purpose and joined the very monsters they swore to oppose.<br /> <br /> <br /> There is also the <b>Dragonblooded</b>, who are obsessed with the study of magic and previously held the position of strongest lineage, before their empire collapsed. Since then, they have adopted an isolationist approach towards the outside world.<br /> <br /> As well as the <b>Exiled House</b>, who boast the greatest martial prowess among their order of honorable warriors. Rumors have accused them of being allegedly responsible for a great act of betrayal, that lead to the downfall of the previous vampire nation, forcing the surviving lineages to retreat into the shadows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 09-18-2026, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-18T21:46:30-07:00","id":1564172,"title":"","content":"I'm personally looking forward to the latest seasons of my favorite shows on the History Channel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://foru